class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T12:44:21-07:00","id":1133119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1127469-fan-group-pdf?p=1132997#post1132997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do we have their Undertaking Skills?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Insofar, we have both the Talents and Frailties of the Chameleon and the Bogeyman Undertaking, However, we do not have their write-up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T14:16:28-07:00","id":1133157,"title":"","content":"How essential is it to have their Undertaking skills? I'd obviously give them Stealth and Subterfuge, but what else? Crafts to represent making disguises? Investigation for researching targets?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T15:06:54-07:00","id":1133180,"title":"","content":"<ul><li>MI18: A gentleman spy sits across from an elegant lady, he is sipping his Martini contentedly while she is very obviously dying of poison.</li> <li>Athenic Church: The ruins of a church with a marble statue of Athena where the alter should be. Owls roost on every available surface.</li> <li>Hakollel shel Hamerkava: A rabbi and a Golem, teacher and student, stand at a desk reading a Torah scroll side by side.</li> <li>Soci\u00e9t\u00e9 d\u2019Had\u00e8s: A caver in the middle of exploring the Underworld.</li> <li>The Baker Street Irregulars: The traditional string covered detective's board.</li> <li>The Reality Hackers: A religious shrine, more esoteric than traditional (e.g. kahballah rather than a crucifix or Star of David), the centrepiece of the shrine is some home-made looking computer equipment.</li> <li>The Order of St. Anthony: A field of graves stretches as far as the eye can see. In the foreground a shovel sticks out of the Earth.</li> <li>The Staff of Janus: A simple stone wall with a wooden gate in an empty field. The gate is covered in vines.</li> <li>Knights Errant: An ordinary bunk bed, like you'd find at any youth hostel. The Holy Grail sits on the top bunk, and a dragon's tail curls around the floor guarding it.</li> <li>KSI-21: A radio tower in the middle of a blizzard.</li> <li>Bastet's Beloved: A women and a cat are cornered by a monster (maybe a vampire) in a dark alleyway. More cats can be seen walking into the alleyway or climbing over the walls.</li> <li>Ride to Damascus: A child or children with are sitting reading an enormous tome and looking happy. Surrounding them is a whole host of monsters, from Beasts' Horrors to more human evils like an abusive parent. A symbolic barrier divides the child(ren) from the monsters.</li> <li>Hearth of Hestia: An ordinary 21<sup>st</sup> century fireplace, fully lit.</li> <li>Sentinal/Warden: A trapdoor with a thick padlock and a bloodied weapon (preferably a baseball bat) resting atop it.</li> <li>Harpy/Alpha: Something like the burn book from mean girls rests on a table, surrounded by photos of high school students. Several photos have been covered with an X, indicating that they're dead.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> So here's the rest of them <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I tried to keep them a bit simpler and to avoid protagonists where I could based on how you interpreted the last one, but there were a few where I couldn't think of any without charachters.<br /> <br /> I took the liberty of posting the pic for Llannerch Athrawon in their thread; and while I was at it I tidied up their Status sections which was always a flaw in their write up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T15:43:22-07:00","id":1133195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1127469-fan-group-pdf?p=1133157#post1133157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How essential is it to have their Undertaking skills? I'd obviously give them Stealth and Subterfuge, but what else? Crafts to represent making disguises? Investigation for researching targets?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't recall if there were any inspirations for the Chameleon, but I believe that Angela Baker from Sleepaway Camp might work. Another inspiration (though he's more of a grey-area protagonist than a full-blown slasher) is Agent 47 from the Hitman series. With Angela, one of the things that she did was masquerade as a camp councilor as well as a police officer in the sequels. With Agent 47, he is encouraged to disguise himself as one of the many workers in the location that his target is located.<br /> <br /> Unsure what to pull inspiration from for the Bogeyman.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Splash Art for The DiFillipo Family done; going to work on SG-14 and then work on a lion's share of TheKingsRaven's concepts. Actually thinking of skipping splash arts for the Slashers and instead providing a character art (mainly just a heavily edited picture but it'll be something).<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/T7BORnt.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </