kers in the location that his target is located.<br /> <br /> Unsure what to pull inspiration from for the Bogeyman.</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing to keep in mind about Chameleons is that the core concept is not disguises, in fact they're not nessacarially good at disguising themselves. The core of the Undertaking is that they don't have much in the way of identity, and because they don't have much identity the world ignores them.<br /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-24-2017, 04:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T02:00:56-07:00","id":1133305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1127469-fan-group-pdf?p=1133299#post1133299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing to keep in mind about Chameleons is that the core concept is not disguises, in fact they're not nessacarially good at disguising themselves. The core of the Undertaking is that they don't have much in the way of identity, and because they don't have much identity the world ignores them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah. Okay. <br /> <br /> Tossing up a different inspiration: Jean-Baptiste Grenouille from Perfume (a man with an extraordinary sense of smell but lacks an odor himself, making others subconsciously ignore him as an individual; he becomes a killer that preserves the scents of those he kills)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T02:53:02-07:00","id":1133310,"title":"","content":"That's fitting. It really is a shame we lost the origonal write up, it was damn good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T07:50:34-07:00","id":1133370,"title":"","content":"Ok, so stealth and subterfuge still works. Others could be Larceny, Survival, Streetwise, Investigation and maybe Occult for the Bogeyman. Don't remember if Scourges get new undertaking skills","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T13:43:09-07:00","id":1133534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1127469-fan-group-pdf?p=1133370#post1133370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, so stealth and subterfuge still works. Others could be Larceny, Survival, Streetwise, Investigation and maybe Occult for the Bogeyman. Don't remember if Scourges get new undertaking skills</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> From the Slasher splatbook, it looks like Rippers usually have 8 Undertaking Skills and Scourges add 2 more. The only one to break that pattern is Avenger-Legend, which only adds Occult.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Speaking of Slashers, I wanted a break from art and wrote up a Ripper and Scourge.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Minder (Ripper)</b><br /><br /> <i>\u201cAll my little children are playing by my rules. Keep this up and you\u2019ll have a great big supper tonight.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> When a murder kills their victims, it\u2019s usually out of some sort of hatred; resentment builds up to a boiling point or revenge calls out from their heart. When a Minder kills their victims, they\u2019ll always be sure to point out that it was because of their love. They only want the best for their special one and they\u2019ll make sure that their special one will act and behave exactly how they should. If they raise a complaint, they get a lash across the rear. If they raise a concern, they get a strike across the face. If they raise a hand, they get a broken wrist. But it\u2019s only because their Minder knows what\u2019s best.<br /> Minders are an insidious thing. The love and kindness that they show their victims are entirely genuine and sincere but the sudden flash of violence and sadism is all the more true. And to the Minder, both the care and the pain they give their victims are entirely because their victims deserve every little bit of it. The poor little babies need a soft hand to bring them into this harsh world but a strong fist to make sure they don\u2019t fall to the dirty, terrible vices that the Minder disapproves of.<br /> And the punishments they give is nothing more but a reminder that the Minder has the final say. If idle hands wander, the Minder will make sure that every little bone is broken so they can wander no longer. If a foul word is uttered, the Minder will make sure the acid burns smoothly to rid that voice of any bad words. And should their sweetie even think of fighting back, the Minder will make sure that their little bodies rest comfortably as they fill their body with the killing drink.<br /> As long as their wards respect their Minder\u2019s authority, the Minder will care for them, watching over them like a mother hen and ensuring that they will be nice and safe. No pain, no tears, just nice and still, perfectly safe. The world around them slowly fading out as they dream the eternal dream.<br /> <b>Background:</b> Fundamentally, Minders revolve around their control. Perhaps they grew up in an environment where their autonomy was stripped away and given to someone in a position of authority. Maybe their lack of control on circumstances outside of their grasp led to embitterment and a need to exert their opinions. Or maybe they were given full control over the life and needs of a person and relished in that fact. Whatever the case, Minders desire to put themselves in a situation where their victims are unable to act for themselves and need an outside force to help them survive.<br /> Hunters that become Minders are often retired and acting mentor to the next generation. They know the cost of incompetence and fear for the safety of their wards\u2019 Cell. They lash out because they know that even a moment of inattention could cause casualties across the board. Gradually and subtly, they become less understanding and more dominating; they weed out the problematic hunters and push up their favorites, punishing the dissenters and rewarding the good children. Once their punishments become fatal, they have completed their conversion to a Minder.<br /> Self-made Minders often start off with good intentions; they are actual parents with high expectations for their children and snap when they fail or they\u2019re devoted lovers who push for their partner to fix their lives. Some are nurses that committed mercy killings to save their patients from suffering, others are teachers that honestly believe that sparing the rod will spoil the child. However the case, this does not absolve the Minder of their actions; their actions are abusive and reprehensible, scarring the victims that make it out alive.<br /> Surprisingly, Minders may possibly have the lowest turn-out rate when it comes to murders out of all Slashers. Their modus operandi revolves around entrapping one or more individuals and slowly gaining access to various facets of their life, often putting their victims under their thumb for years before finally disposing of them once their victims decide to fight back. Some Minders even prefer to lobotomize their victims, leaving them alive but utterly and entirely dependent on the Minder.<br /> <b><i>Inspirations:</i></b> <i>Annie Wilkes (Misery), Yamazaki Asami (Audition), Blue Jones (Sucker Punch)</i><br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Manipulation or Composure<br /> <b>Undertaking Skills: </b>Investigation, Medicine, Brawl, Weaponry, Empathy, Persuasion, Socialization, Subterfuge<br /> <b>Talent \u2013 It\u2019s For Your Own Good</b>: Minders care for their ward, for better or worse, and when a Minder wants to keep their wards in line, they make sure that the sting is a reminder. Whenever a Minder inflicts any form damage on their target using their fists, a melee weapon, or some form of physical torture, they instill a fear that digs itself deep into the victim\u2019s mind. Against their specific victims, Minders automatically inflict the Insensate Tilt. Against outsiders, the Minder rolls Manipulation + Presence against the target\u2019s Resolve + Composure.<br /> <b>Frailty \u2013 I\u2019m So Proud of You:</b> If there is anything that will take a Minder\u2019s thoughts out of their desire to punish, it\u2019s seeing their ward behave properly. Anyone who has spent a scene or more in the presence of a Minder instinctively knows the Minder\u2019s Virtue. Furthermore, when someone acts in a way or manner that fulfills the Minder\u2019s Virtue, it fills the Minder with pride and happiness. The Minder considers the target to be a non-threat to both the Minder and their victim until the target acts in a hostile manner. This may only occur once per person per scene and will not prevent others from being considered non-threats.<br /> <br /> <b>VASCU Case Study: The Good Mother</b><br /> <i>From an interview with Isaac G, victim of the Good Mother:</i><br /> <i>\u201c\u2026there were times when she would purposefully starve us because we made too much noise going up and down the basement stairs or because we looked outside of the window for too long. Sometimes one of us would misbehave and we all would be punished because she wanted to teach us a lesson.</i><br /> <i>\u201cI remember when she made us watch when Caroline took a slice of bread with her. Mother mixed up some bleach with ipecac syrup because she wanted to wash out Caroline\u2019s body. Said she wanted that piece of bread back. Caroline didn\u2019t stop throwing up until blood was running down her nose and onto her shirt. Then Mother made her clean up the vomit with her clothes.</i><br /> <i>\u201c\u2026my hand. I used to play the piano. Was going to school to be a classical performer. She\u2026she told me that I kept playing the wrong notes. I knew I was playing it right. I KNEW I was. But she didn\u2019t like it. Said I went too high or too low or too fast or too slow. I-my hand\u2026she used the hot water be-because she knew I wanted to play b-b-but\u2026then she held my h-h-hand in the\u2026the drawer. A-a-and she\u2026she\u2026\u201d</i><br /> <i>Interview cut short due to Isaac G suffering from a panic attack and going catatonic. Follow-up scheduled for two weeks after recovery.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> -----<br /> <br /> <b>Master (Scourge)</b><br /><br /> <i>\u201cDogs aren\u2019t supposed to talk.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> While a Minder\u2019s game is about control, there is a twisted logic behind the Minder\u2019s behavior; the Minder sees their victims as an equal (somewhat) and wants to see their victims happy. With a Master, there is no desire to treat their victims with any sort of respect; they are the Master and their victims are nothing more than animals that bow at their feet. Rewards are few and infrequent while punishments are more proactive than reactive. They want to keep their pets, their dogs, in line and the most effective way to do so is with the fear of pain.<br /> Stripped of their compassion, Masters have no true love for their victims. Maybe they feel some sort of pity for such a creature or a carnal desire for their flesh; Masters only care for their pets because they are useful, despite their disgusting figure and pathetic displays of emotion. They are entirely divorced from their victims, having no meaningful connection to the naked animals slobbering all over themselves. These dogs only exist for the entertainment of the Master<br /> Masters thrive on the fact that they rule over a lesser being; even if they do not hold any exceptional power outside of this domain, Masters are more than willing to create the illusion that they alone are the core to their victim\u2019s lives. Their pets have no need to think or want; their Master holds their leash and will make sure that they are given a life that they deserve.<br /> And they, the Masters, are always looking for new pets to add to their collection. As long as there are dogs willing to beg, the Masters will come to round them up and place them in the kennel, along with the rest.<br /> <b>Background:</b> When a Minder finds a new victim, they are overcome with a desire to protect. Minders, however twisted they are, work on an internal logic that they themselves are good people and are capable of rearing good people with their victims. They may harm but it\u2019s only so that their victims can heal; it\u2019s all because of their perverted compassion.<br /> Masters don\u2019t care for their victims. Masters consider themselves to be on a level above and beyond that which dogs are even able to manage. Minders that begin to see themselves as better than their victims or tire of having to care for all of their children are on the path to becoming a Master. Once they realize that their control over their wards can be further abused to force their victims to act against their own will, they start their descent.<br /> The creation of a Master outside of being a slasher is surprisingly easy. A cult leader who can manipulate their herd into massive rallies and violent riots has all the shades of being a Master. Likewise, the CEO of an established company that sends out lackeys to harass and potentially drive others to suicide is more or less a Master awaiting the inevitable breakdown into pure sociopathy.<br /> Their ability to not only dominate but eliminate any sense of self from their victims is what makes the Master a Scourge. Their victims blindly worship their Master because that is the only way that they feel any form of satisfaction. At their Master\u2019s command they will act; if their Master wishes to kill one off for entertainment, they will gladly tear one another apart if it pleases. The invisible collar around their necks is what binds them to their Master\u2019s will.<br /> <b><i>Inspirations:</i></b><i> Sofia Lamb (Bioshock 2), Justine (Amnesia: The Dark Descent), Lola Stone (The Loved Ones),</i><br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Manipulation or Composure<br /> <b>Undertaking Skills:</b> Investigation, Medicine, Politics, Brawl, Weaponry, Empathy, Intimidation, Persuasion, Socialization, Subterfuge<br /> <b>Talent \u2013 The Hand that Feeds You:</b> A dog should obey its Master. Whenever a Master captures a victim, they impart the idea that the Master is the only thing that matters in the world to them. The Master\u2019s specific victims are unable to access Social merits relating to individuals outside of their relationship with the Master (Mentors, Retainers, True Friends, etc.). Furthermore, the Master\u2019s specific victims under the Insensate Tilt as applied by the It\u2019s For Your Own Good become fiercely loyal to the Master and their commands, acting with hostility to those who threaten or harm their Master; they will blindly follow the Master\u2019s command no matter how dangerous. They also gain the persistent Amnesia Condition that pertains to any memory before they met the Master. This effect does not occur to outsiders affected with by the Insensate Tilt.<br /> Victims can be deprogrammed with an extended action. As long as the victim is away from the Master\u2019s presence, a third party may roll Wits + Empathy to attempt to rehabilitate the victim. The process takes one week per roll and requires a total of 10 + the Master\u2019s Manipulation + Composure to fully deprogram as well as remove the Amnesia Condition. If the victim makes contact with the Master at any time, the process is reset.<br /> <b>Frailty \u2013 If I Can\u2019t Have You: </b>Masters are empowered by their control; denial affects them in ways they refuse to acknowledge. Whenever a Master fails either a Social roll or an attempt at using the It\u2019s For Your Own Good Talent on a target, they suffer from the Deprived Condition in regards to the target\u2019s submission to the Master\u2019s control. Furthermore, as long as the Deprived Condition remains, the Master begins to suffer from a self-destructive streak; they take out their frustration on objects, pets, anything in order to vent. The Master cannot regain Willpower and suffers 1 point of Bashing damage for each day that the target spends away from the Master. This effect ends once the Master resolves the Deprived Condition by making the target submit to their power.<br /> <br /> <b>VASCU Case Study: </b>\u201cGod\u201d<br /> <i>Hastily scrawled across the walls and floor in a containment cell by Jane Doe, rescued 12/5:</i><br /> <i>CAST OUT OF EDEN GOD ANGRY GOD WAITING</i><br /> <i>ONE KING ONE RULER ONE GOD</i><br /> <i>SHE IS SUN SHE IS LIGHT SHE IS LIFE</i><br /> <i>DOG OBEY GOD OR GOD PUNISH DOG</i><br /> <i>OUT IS SODOM ONLY OUTSIDE BAD OUTSIDE FEAR</i><br /> <i>GOD SAVE DOG AND DOG OBEY GOD</i><br /> <i>SHE FEED DOG SHE CLEAN DOG SHE WARM DOG</i><br /> <i>WANT EDEN SAFE FOR DOG EDEN WHERE GOD WAITS</i><br /> <i>DOG WANT EDEN DOG FEAR SODOM DOG FEAR OUT</i><br /> <i>GOD SAVE DOG</i><br /> <i>DOG WANT GOD</i><br /> <i>SAVE DOG WANT GOD</i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1417,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","user":"Reaper Verse","date":". 08-25-2017, 12:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T07:34:17-07:00","id":1133784,"title":"","content":"Rough outline for the Chameleon, what does it need?<br /> <br /> <b>Chameleon</b><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cI\u2019ve just got one of those faces.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> Robin Dunbar proposed a concept that the human brain only has the cognitive ability to maintain roughly 150 stable relationships. While some have criticized it the theory on the basis that this ignores the many social connections necessary to build up human civilization at all, no one can deny that they all have many people they can remember and care enough about to interact with on a regular basis. Everyone else is a face in the crowd, shifting through the observer\u2019s life with hardly a thought about the anonymous beings walking about around them.<br /> <br /> What happens to the people who manage through no fault of their own to slip between the cracks of everyone else\u2019s sphere? Who somehow go nearly their entire lives without close friends or romances? Some just go on with their lives, quietly living as they do and ignoring the loneliness that aches at their hearts. Others feel offended by this, angered that their lives are somehow unseen and unheard by those around them. Maybe it started in childhood when they realized no one noticed when they broke a rule and got away with it. Perhaps it carried on later into adulthood when they finally broke and went to meet new people in the most lethal way possible.<br /> <br /> A Chameleon is aptly named, able to slip in and out of any location simply by not drawing attention to themselves. Their targets may think they were nothing more than an accidental bump into a shoulder on the subway, a passing nod to a stranger on the street, but to the Chameleon these run ins were their determination for who they would kill next. Some of them kill because they feel slighted in some way by their victims. That they were being mocked in some way by their new target, walking around parading their value in front of the slasher. Others see it as an obsession, not unlike a stalker finally killing the very person they have their obsession centered on. If they can\u2019t be the only focus on their target\u2019s attention, no one else can be.<br /> <br /> What makes a Chameleon dangerous is that they easily blend in anywhere. They\u2019re the \u201ckiller cop\u201d, putting flashing lights on the roof of his car and buying a prop badge to lure out the unsuspecting motorists he kidnaps and kills. He\u2019s a lowly janitor, fired months ago but still coming in to work because no one cares enough to check his badge to see it\u2019s out of date. All he is, is a face in the crowd that can\u2019t be seen. It\u2019s not that he\u2019s a master of disguise, in fact many of the chameleons captured barely have what could be considered a \u201cwardrobe\u201d at all. Their \u201cgift\u201d is that the rest of the world simply considers them invisible.<br /> <br /> <b>Background:</b> Chameleons don\u2019t have what could be considered a \u201cprocess\u201d for choosing a victim. Most of the time the victim only knows the chameleon as, \u201cThat one guy\u201d they see at work or in their apartment complex. To the chameleons, their victims is another human being that pays no attention to them. It may be that the chameleon considers them someone that mocks their \u201cignoring\u201d the slasher, or maybe they\u2019re the people who are the friends and family of the one person that shows the chameleon any sign that they notice them. In either case, the chameleon is a patient predator. They slowly move themselves into the lives of those they follow without ever being noticed as best they can. They track their targets, trailing them to and from work, about their lives, and inevitably either growing envious of the fact that other people care about them, or of the others who spend time with the person who shows them the attention they so sorely lack. Like their namesakes, Chameleon slashers are swift killers. Once their prey is utterly at their mercy, the slasher strikes without mercy.<br /> <br /> Not many hunters wind up as Chameleons, they\u2019re ingratiated too greatly with their cells to be unnoticed in the same way these poor souls are. The people who wind up becoming Chameleons are more often than not just people. Ignored by everyone around them, anyone who does show them even the slightest bit of attention can immediately find their lives turned upside down as their loved ones, coworkers, even employees at stores they frequent are killed off or up and vanish.<br /> <br /> More twisted Chameleons realize that their only real interaction with humanity is via murder. Rather than wallowing in their loneliness, these killers strike out to find those they can kill. Such killers can hound the police for years, most famously in the case of a person known only as \u201cThe Smiley Face Killer\u201d. Only two retired detectives have managed to put the information together that links the murders, but the FBI officially stated, \u201c\u2026The vast majority of these instances appear to be alcohol-related drownings.\u201d In the background, VASCU desperately tries to catch up with the Smiley Face Killer, knowing that their target can be anyone, anywhere, and they wouldn\u2019t even know it until they find another body in a lake or river.<br /> <br /> <b>Inspirations:</b> Zartan (G.I. Joe: Rise of Cobra); False Face (Batman); Carlos the Jackal (Day of the Jackal)<br /> <br /> <b>Talent: </b>A Thousand Masks<br /> <br /> <b>Frailty:</b> Telltale Sign<br /> <br /> <i>VASCU Case File: \u201cThe Newsboy\u201d</i><br /> <br /> <i>Notes from Det. Frank Bianchi, NYPD</i><br /> <br /> <i>Uniforms found another last night. Young girl, couldn\u2019t be older than 22, no ID just like the others. Stabbed multiple times, left to bleed out, posed to look like she was homeless. Lucky for us, the spot where she was left actually belonged to a bum.</i><br /> <br /> <i>The captain\u2019s getting on my ass about this one, but we don\u2019t fucking know where to start. Every witness doesn\u2019t remember anyone really standing out. They don\u2019t remember anyone talking to the victim, her friends don\u2019t mention anyone following her the past few days, it\u2019s all turning up empty.</i><br /> <br /> <i>The only connection between the victims is that they all stopped at the same news stand to grab a magazine or newspaper. Owner said he didn\u2019t see anything suspicious either, no one tracking them or acting like they were too interested.</i><br /> <br /> <i>Christ, they\u2019re gonna have my shield if we don\u2019t figure this one out soon. I\u2019ll go back to the stand today, see if the guy might\u2019ve remembered something since the last time we spoke.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":483,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","user":"Flyboy254","date":". 08-26-2017, 04:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T11:21:49-07:00","id":1133874,"title":"","content":"That looks pretty good.<br /> <br /> The official write-ups for Slashers usually include a Background section where they profile the Undertaking with pseudo-psychology and talk about what causes the Slasher to become a Slasher and then talk about what kinds of people are more likely to become that Undertaking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T11:39:07-07:00","id":1133890,"title":"","content":"It is a good start. And yes, it need text on how they become a Slasher and why they kill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T11:39:19-07:00","id":1133891,"title":"","content":"Dammit, knew I forgot something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T18:17:11-07:00","id":1134008,"title":"","content":"Throwing together some Sterotypes and Hunters for some of the unfinished factions.<br /> <br /> <b>The Bookhounds of London</b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><ul><li><i>Ashwood Abbey - </i>Lots of money and intensely curious about the occult but far too lazy to actually put effort into learning about it. The perfect clients.</li> <li><i>Ride to Damascus</i> - There is no doubt their books contain arcane power but they reads like MLK edited Chicken Soup for the Soul. There's no market for this.</li> <li><i>Aegis Kai Doru - </i>We could probably make a tidy profit selling to them if they would stop trying to stab every dealer they come across.</li> <li><i>MI18 - </i>Operator Manuals and blueprints for bio-mechanical brain parasites powered by the victim's day dreams are sort of magical. In an Arthur C. Clarke sort of way. </li> </ul></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <b>The Fire Starters</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><ul><li>You lost everything in the '09 crash. Your house, your car, your marriage. You aren't sure about this murder business yet but you're desperate and that wish sounds good.</li> <li>You've been burning buildings down for years before one spoke to you. You think you might be going crazy but the fire's orders have been fun so you keep going. You're almost ready for your wish but you aren't really sure that you want the fun to stop.</li> <li>Your brother was killed in a mugging years ago. Last week he, or something that looked like him paid you a visit. Later that night as you watched your home burn the flames thanked you for killing him and said there were more lying creatures like that thing wearing your brother's face out there.</li> </ul><ul><li><i>The Long Night - </i>After I burned that church preacher and all these biblethumpers took to the streets en masse looking for &quot;the witch&quot; responsible. I'm scared of what they'd do to me if I told them about their late-pastor's secret stash.</li> <li><i>Habibti Ma - </i>Rumor is that a bunch of these so called do gooders got an entire cell of us institutionalized in Egypt. The Hospital went up in flames before anyone could get any answers from them.</li> <li><i>Lucifuge - </i>Say &quot;L'Enfant Diaboliques&quot; one more time, I dare you.</li> <li><i>The Hunt Club - </i>Everyone likes to lump us in with these sick freaks. Sometimes when the fire asks me to kill I wonder if they're right to. </li> </ul></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9065-darkblade","name":"Darkblade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T01:48:45-07:00","id":1134083,"title":"","content":"Just edited the Chameleon information, any better?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T08:22:05-07:00","id":1134147,"title":"","content":"Looks pretty solid to me. Well done. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T09:02:49-07:00","id":1134152,"title":"","content":"So for Boogeyman, should we go for &quot;Incorporeal&quot; or &quot;Functionally Invisible&quot;.?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T10:15:22-07:00","id":1134171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1127469-fan-group-pdf?p=1134152#post1134152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So for Boogeyman, should we go for &quot;Incorporeal&quot; or &quot;Functionally Invisible&quot;.?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I believe the answer would be &quot;yes&quot;.<br /> <br /> To elaborate, the transition from Ripper to Scourge seems to be a loss of something that keeps the Ripper grounded in humanity while empowering them with a power that makes them more supernatural in nature. Geniuses that become too enraptured in their own thoughts and ideologies transcends to a Maniac, Avengers that hunt down their quarry too efficiently become the horror stories that are Legends. For Chameleons, it seems that their core is that they are unnoticed; they are the &quot;nobody&quot;, the blurriest face among blurry faces. However, they are still a &quot;person&quot;, so to speak; they have a presence that is noticed in the physical realm like a home under a pseudonym or a membership among fishing enthusiasts. Despite them being beneath notice, people can still prove that the Chameleon is a person.<br /> <br /> With Bogeymen (especially considering their Talent and Frailty), they go completely off the grid. They aren't A nobody, they are nobody; they leave no footprint or paper trail, they have no home to their name or a notable persona. They just aren't other than a Bogeyman, like a Legend but less embroidered in their story. If anything, I would compare them to something like an infamous name on the internet that searches for their screen name in search engines to figure out who is talking about them; they thrive in their lack of identity but can be warded off by forcibly bringing them back into reality by speaking their &quot;true name&quot; (playing into the Still Attached Frailty).<br /> <br /> I can't name an example that follows the Bogeyman precisely. If anything, Daniella from Haunting Grounds has a tick that functions like the Still Attached Frailty. Daniella is a maid that chases down the protagonist because she (Daniella) sees herself as incomplete, wanting to harvest a part from the protagonist. Effectively, she is unstoppable; however, if she is led to a mirror or other reflective surface, she halts and shrieks in fury, effectively immobilizing her for a considerable amount of time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T10:35:52-07:00","id":1134178,"title":"","content":"See, I was thinking of this MotW from the X-Files. Maybe not <i>exactly</i> as kill-happy as a boogeyman, but certainly fits with the idea that he's been forgotten by the world, has one or two who still remember him, and can effectively go anywhere he pleases.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://x-files.wikia.com/wiki/Nathaniel_Teager\" target=\"_blank\">http://x-files.wikia.com/wiki/Nathaniel_Teager</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T10:49:36-07:00","id":1134182,"title":"","content":"has the new pdf been created yet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T10:56:40-07:00","id":1134185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1127469-fan-group-pdf?p=1134178#post1134178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, I was thinking of this MotW from the X-Files. Maybe not <i>exactly</i> as kill-happy as a boogeyman, but certainly fits with the idea that he's been forgotten by the world, has one or two who still remember him, and can effectively go anywhere he pleases.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://x-files.wikia.com/wiki/Nathaniel_Teager\" target=\"_blank\">http://x-files.wikia.com/wiki/Nathaniel_Teager</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That definitely fits into the supernatural status of the Bogeyman in my opinion.<br /> <br /> Maybe another concept could be Henry Creedlow from Bruiser, though he can flip between Avenger and Chameleon; he's a weak-willed salaryman who is spurred into murder when he loses his face. He is surprisingly adept at avoiding suspicion and manages to kill several individuals who have wronged him, &quot;curing&quot; him of his blank face. It's implied near the end that he will continue to lose his face whenever he is driven to kill.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1127469-fan-group-pdf?p=1134182#post1134182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">has the new pdf been created yet?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't believe so. I haven't actually published a PDF as of yet and I don't believe Flyboy254 has published anything yet either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1417,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","user":"Reaper Verse","date":". 08-26-2017, 02:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T11:08:53-07:00","id":1134191,"title":"","content":"I have absolutely no knowledge on how to make a PDF, I'm just trying to organize this project and guide it to a finished state.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T11:46:34-07:00","id":1134204,"title":"","content":"If you make one big document in a google drive you can just download it as a PDF.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1127469-fan-group-pdf?p=1134083#post1134083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just edited the Chameleon information, any better?</div> </div> </div> </div>I still think it needs more, mind if I try my hand?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T11:52:15-07:00","id":1134206,"title":"","content":"The floor is yours.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b> Putting these here so Reaper can grab them and add them for the slasher section.<br /> <br /> <b>Splinter </b>(Ripper)<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Sorry, I couldn\u2019t stop myself</i><br /> <br /> Splinters don\u2019t want to kill. At least a part of them doesn\u2019t. The same can\u2019t be said for the other part. The other part kills like it is absolutely nothing, while the peaceful side is left to deal with the body. Splinters are usually very normal people. In fact they\u2019re nicer than normal. Then there\u2019s a part of them that becomes disgusted by the niceness, disgusted by the fact that people are just and kind in an unkind and unjust world. When this part of them becomes angry enough, it simply takes over.<br /> <br /> Splinters have a short time to plan before the good side realizes what they have done, so they must plan quickly. They have to improvise. They don\u2019t design traps, but instead look for places where the traps are already made for them. Perhaps there is a prostitute on an empty street, or a man that lives alone in an extremely flammable house. They don\u2019t just club people to death; they look at their surroundings first. They know that no one would suspect their other side, so they get the bodies into the bathtub and buy a ton of lye, leaving their bewildered \u201cgood side\u201d to do the rest. <br /> <br /> Splinters usually do what they do because they suppressed a darker side of themselves. Maybe they were abused as a child, or maybe the anger management that turned their lives around somehow backfired. Maybe they were just too <i>nice </i>and needed to know how it felt to be something else, but suppressed the memory of all their kills because someone like them simply wouldn\u2019t do something like that. It\u2019s also probable that it was just some neurological problem. A hunter that became a Splinter probably started out facing something so horrifying that they began to refuse to believe in the supernatural, but there is still a part of them that can\u2019t get enough of the killing.<br /> <br /> Splinters would seem more redeemable than other slashers if they weren\u2019t so insane. The good side is definitely a potential ally, seeing as he needs all the help he can get fighting the bad side. But sometimes his own psyche can be too big of an obstacle for him to handle no matter how much help he has.<br /> Splinters always have high wits because they need to be able to think and act quickly and they almost always have high composure because killing comes so naturally to the bad side and the good side still needs to maintain some of his sanity. They rely on any attributes their good side has to kill. <br /> <br /> Attribute: Wits<br /> <br /> Undertaking Skills: Weaponry, Investigation, Science, Crafts, Stealth, Subterfuge, Persuasion, Athletics<br /> <br /> Talent: Zen-like: The dark side of a Splinter is usually either irrational or evil, so either way the threat of death doesn\u2019t faze him. His calmness makes him very accurate and gives him the ability to think on his feet better than most. He takes his time with every shot and is able to make use of what he has Splinters are always calm when murdering and think nothing of it, so they are given a +2 bonus to targeted attacks and take no penalties to mental rolls.<br /> <br /> Frailty: Time Bomb: The dark side of the Splinter can\u2019t come out whenever he wants. Something needs to trigger it and after it is triggered, it can only last for the rest of the scene. It could be triggered by the sight of blood or simply having someone visit his house. When this happens, the Splinter must indulge in their vice before anything else.<br /> <br /> <b>VASCU Case Study: \u201cTwo O\u2019clock\u201d Gunther</b><br /> <i>Transcript of interview between Folsom Prison guards and inmate Lito \u201cM-16\u201d Rodriguez</i><br /> <br /> <i>LR: CO, I\u2019m telling you, you can\u2019t let that fucker out!</i><br /> <br /> <i>Guard: Why Lito? We already know what you\u2019ve done, how much worse can he make it?</i><br /> <br /> <i>LR: It\u2019s not me I\u2019m worried about, it\u2019s the people outside, jefe. He\u2019ll kill them if you don\u2019t put him back inside.</i><br /> <br /> <i>Guard: You mean Gunther? He\u2019s been released on good behavior, he\u2019s served his sentence.</i><br /> <br /> <i>LR: It\u2019s not him I\u2019m worried about, it\u2019s Two-O\u2019clock.</i><br /> <br /> <i>Guard: Who?</i><br /> <br /> <i>LR: I don\u2019t know, jefe, it\u2019s like there a switch in him that flips around two in the morning! He\u2019s a completely different person, like there\u2019s a second person inside.</i><br /> <br /> <i>Guard: You mean dissociative identity disorder?</i><br /> <br /> <i>LR: Whatever, that fuck, those fucks, however many there are, they\u2019re out now. Two-O\u2019clock told me, he\u2019s gonna start killing kids when he\u2019s done.</i><br /> <br /> <i>Guard: That\u2019s enough, get him back to his cell.</i><br /> <br /> <i>Note: Disturbingly, disappearances of minors has indeed shot up in the area where Mr. Gunther has moved. We may need to alert the Feds on this information, but we\u2019ll wait until we get more information before we make a move.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Split</b> (Scourge)<br /> <br /> <i>Kill me? That\u2019s not happening. You need me</i><br /> <br /> While a Splinter has a light side and a dark side, they\u2019re still the same person even if they never want to acknowledge it. They share a name and they essentially look the same, but with Lunatics, the two parts become so different that they are nothing like the same man. The posture, the voice, and the facial expressions, usually coupled with an affinity for disguise make the two sides unrecognizable. At this point, they no longer think the same and the struggle between the light and dark sides becomes an all-out war.<br /> <br /> Splits often think more about the long term than Splinters, but they still realize the importance of improvisation. Splits will often try to differentiate themselves from their good side to the point where they would go to places that their good side wouldn\u2019t even consider going to. Maybe even places the good side despises and swore he would never set foot in again. They also enjoy seeing the fear in their victims\u2019 eyes a lot more then Splinters, who are usually a lot more detached. Splits also realize the importance of concealed weapons and try to hide these weapons in all of the good side\u2019s things. Maybe they\u2019ll add a bit of weight to their walking cane or put a couple razor blades in their pockets. Splits have gotten a little cocky because they know that whenever anything gets rough, they can change into something which is nothing like them. <br /> <br /> Splinters cross the line into becoming Splits when the two sides become completely irreconcilable. Splinters are still basically themselves when they give into the bad side, just a more murderous version. Both sides want to differentiate from the other and as the dark side become more consumed by his vice, he gets cocky. There\u2019s no such thing as a low profile anymore, no hiding in broken down motels or towers or trying to look ordinary. Lunatics can also be created by supernatural means, such as being affected by mind spells or consuming some strange elixir.<br /> <br /> Splinters struggle with themselves, but each side at least tries to consider the other side. The dark side believes that they are in this together and will make it easier for the good side to continue living an ordinary life, or at least try to put him in a position that isn\u2019t so bad. The good side will believe that his other side is curable and someday the two sides may be reconcilable. Splits just stop caring or sometimes take pride in sabotaging the other\u2019s life. If the good side can\u2019t bring himself to turn the other side in, he will constantly leave evidence and assist in the case. The dark side will gleefully sabotage the good side\u2019s relationships and terrorize his friends. This war keeps escalating, but no one seems to win in the end.<br /> <br /> Attribute: Wits<br /> <br /> Undertaking Skills: Weaponry, Investigation, Science, Crafts, Stealth, Subterfuge, Persuasion, Athletics, Intimidate, Socialize<br /> <br /> Talent: Two-Faced: Splits have two distinct personalities and appearances, which are completely irreconcilable. They do not think the same way or have any of the same habits. Their abilities, virtues, and vices are the same, but they manifest in different ways. Any attempt to track, investigate, or see through a Lunatic\u2019s disguise are penalized by 3.<br /> <br /> Frailty: Self-Loathing- Each half of a Split despises the other half with a great intensity. Every time the Split seriously harms or helps someone out, he makes two resolve plus composure roles. If the first role exceeds the second, the other side of the Split gains control and can use it to sabotage his alter ego\u2019s life.<br /> <br /> <b>VASCU Case Study: Michael Franklin/Victor Devaroux</b><br /> <i>Taken from the journal of Mr. Franklin</i><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cI can\u2019t take this anymore. Victor, that bastard, he nearly sent me to prison last night! He gave me control just as the young woman bled out over me. I tried to save her, staunch the bleeding, but he\u2019d cut too deep. Damn him, that\u2019s the third.</i><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cI\u2019ve thought about ways to kill him without him knowing, but he always takes control just at the right time. When the threat is immediate, he pops out and laughs, I can still hear it from the last time. He just dropped the coffee on the floor, and Mary just mopped it up with a smile. I have made sure to write her into my will, but Victor, he\u2019s tried to have it changed by impersonating me. Thank the Lord that my lawyer is not as simple as Victor believes everyone else to be.</i><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cBut I think I have the solution now. Victor knows about killing, but not about saving. It sickens me to say this, but perhaps I can have him kill someone with HIV. It must be done, immediately, before he can stop himself.</i><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cJesus forgive me for this sin, but there is little other way. I have thought of time bombs or fires, but he would know then too. He\u2019d leap out a window, or throw the bomb into the street. Mary would be endangered, and I will not have my wife made a victim by my own evils.</i><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cWait. That\u2019s it. Something he won\u2019t suspect. I\u2019m the world\u2019s safest driver. He\u2019ll never see a car accident happen. A sudden swerve into oncoming traffic, a semi\u2026</i><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cI will feel sorry for the driver, but it needs to be done. He\u2019ll be finished at last, and if I\u2019m lucky he\u2019ll die and himself alone. Forgive me Mary for what I must do.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> <b>Stranger</b><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cI\u2026 I need this. I need to be\u2026 complete.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> In his own mind, the Stranger is defined less by what he is, and more by what he is not. For starters, he is not complete. When he looks in the mirror, he does not recognize the person staring back. His skin feels like a mask, his body a cage, confining the true self within. He is a beauty, a beast, a monster, trapped in weak, fallible flesh.<br /> <br /> The Stranger seeks to become whole. He seeks the transformative process, that which will bring forth his true self. He begins a quest for the formula, finding glances of the true self on the faces of others. He stakes his territory with a knife and a gun, seeking revelation in the fear and blood of his victims, trying to find that which will make him complete.<br /> <br /> A young man hires prostitutes, takes them to darkened hotel rooms, then slits their throats with a straight razor. As the blood pulses into his open mouth, he chokes on the bitter taste of copper and longs for the day when he becomes one of the undead, when the blood shall taste as sweet as pure ambrosia. A woman, seeking the strength of a man, kidnaps female-to-male transsexuals and performs autopsies on them, trying to find the form of the rebis, the alchemical marriage of the two genders. A brutish young orphan reads of the nephilim, the abandoned children of treacherous angels, and defiles church altars with the bodies of their priests in an unholy black mass, hoping that the Grigori will see his deeds and assume him into the fold.<br /> <br /> <b>Background</b>: The Stranger\u2019s desire for completion is rooted first and foremost in the denial of his own self. He is not a person \u2013 at least, not as he is now. What he is is weak, and humble, and worthless. It is only through adopting the persona of another that he can come to terms with his own existence and feel like he is more than a shadow on the wall.<br /> <br /> Usually, a Stranger reaches such depths of self-loathing through a period of great trauma. Perhaps he loses his entire family in a freak accident, and blames himself for some perceived weakness that prevented him from coming to their aid. Maybe his childhood was characterized by abuse from a guardian, wherein he was attacked for being a \u201cfreak.\u201d He views himself as a mockery of existence, and wants to find out why other people can just be who they are so easily. The quest to get under another person\u2019s skin may involve him slicing it off and wearing it as a mask.<br /> <br /> A Stranger may begin their career as a hunter out of a desire to get closer to his chosen targets. His research into lycanthropy myths may prove invaluable to a cell that spends their time tracking down werewolves who feed on human flesh\u2026 at least, until his comrades find the bodies, missing pieces of skin that he\u2019s taken to cure into a wolfskin belt of his own. Similarly, a Stranger may be a hunter who has experienced real loss at the hands of monsters. When a partner in his cell is torn to pieces at the claws of a raging vampire, he may wish to claim the heart of the creature\u2019s power for revenge. But the more he finds himself trying to match the monster, the more he comes to empathize its point of view.<br /> <br /> A Stranger is a versatile being, willing to do anything to accomplish his goal. Their Attributes and Skills depend as much upon their quarry as themselves. A man who hunts young women who idle into the forest after dark in an attempt to become a werewolf will favor Physical Attributes and Skills such as Survival and Animal Ken, while a pretty young thing who desires to become the lamia and drive men to ruin will focus on Social Attributes and Skills such as Expression and Persuasion. All Strangers have a strong head for Skills such as Academics, Medicine, Occult, or Science \u2013 they wish to understand their other self, inside and out.<br /> <br /> <b>Inspirations</b>: Martin (<i>Martin</i>), Francis Dolarhyde (<i>Red Dragon</i>), Hedy Carlson (<i>Single White Female</i>), Buffalo Bill (<i>The Silence of the Lambs</i>)<br /> <br /> <b>Attributes</b>: Intelligence, Resolve, Dexterity or Stamina<br /> <br /> <b>Undertaking Skills</b>: Academics, Animal Ken, Investigation, Larceny, Medicine, Streetwise, Survival, Weaponry<br /> <br /> <b>Talent \u2013 Dreams of the Other</b>: The Stranger seeks with all his will to become the persona he holds in his heart. His heart sings as he approaches the quarry, and when the blade finds home, he exults in the revelation that comes with it. When he pursues a target directly related to his goal of apotheosis, he has the option to risk Willpower on the roll, just like a hunter (see Hunter: the Vigil). Furthermore, if he is successful in his hunt and manages to \u201clearn\u201d from his target, he gains a +2 to all rolls to risk Willpower for the next scene. The glory of the revelation fades soon after, however, and he must begin his hunt for perfection again.<br /> <br /> <b>Frailty \u2013 No Heart But Another\u2019s</b>: At his very core, the Stranger seeks to become something else because he has no true sense of identity. His real name is an alias, his face is a mask, and his words are always lies. When the Stranger makes an Expression, Persuasion, or Socialize roll, he makes it at a -3 penalty at all times. If he is pursuing a quarry, he can spend Willpower to offset the penalty and even risk Willpower to ensure great success, but in all other cases, the Stranger\u2019s true emptiness shines through.<br /> <br /> <b>VASCU Case Study: The Tithe-Keeper</b><br /> <br /> <i>From the files of VASCU forensic psychologist Sarah Kepler</i><br /> <br /> <i>When I finally had the chance to sit down for an interview with Jessica Casey, I found a woman very different from what I had expected. Her medical history had indicated a history of manic-depressive behavior, but that was nothing compared to the woman who walked like one of the condemned into the interview area. The scars of past suicide attempts marked her wrists -- one of the cuts still appeared fresh -- and her eyes... her eyes were always clouded. Like she was on the verge of tears.<br /> <br /> &quot;They won't come for me,&quot; was the first thing she said to me, and she didn't want to let it go. With enough poking, I began to get her to talk about her past. Her mother had always told her fairy tales before going to bed, but that had been before the accident. Afterwards, she ended up in the possession of her uncle Francis, who had subjected her to physical and emotional abuse for six years before child services had noticed. Every time I compelled a fact from her, she ended the sentence with, &quot;They won't come for me.&quot;<br /> <br /> The next session, I began by asking her who &quot;they&quot; were, and if they'd had anything to do with the children -- seven young boys and girls, all of whom had been in Casey's care, all of whose seemingly unmarred bodies were found in forests secreted away under trees and in rings of mushrooms. When I broached the topic, she began to break down crying, and said that &quot;they&quot; couldn't hear her here, due to the iron in the walls. She curled up on the floor and cried for her mother -- her <b>true</b> mother, Queen Mab of the Faeries -- until the guards came to take her back to the cell.<br /> <br /> Jessica Casey escaped from her cell on November 1st, 2008, and her absence was not noted until cell inspections that night. Her true whereabouts are still unknown.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Transcendent</b><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cBehold my glory, and despair.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> The only thing more dangerous than a man who kills for his ideals is one who has accomplished them and sees no reason to stop. Through the study of blood, flesh, and death, the Stranger becomes something more than human. They have unlocked the secrets of apotheosis, accomplished their dream, and freed themselves from the cage of meat and bone. They have become Transcendent, and nothing is beyond their limit.<br /> <br /> Some green VASCU agents question why a Stranger would keep killing once he\u2019s attained his own twisted sense of perfection. Those who deal in the cases of the Transcendent know that mere perfection is never enough. For the slasher, the body has gone from cage to altar. It is a wild fire, a mad god, an engine of destruction, something both beautiful and terrible to behold. The Transcendent demands adoration, and like an Old Testament God, is fully willing to strike down the blasphemous to secure the worthy.<br /> <br /> The worst part of dealing with one of the Transcendent is that they serve as testament to an uncomfortable truth \u2013 <i>they were right</i>. What a forensic psychologist might dismiss as delusion or psychosis is proven to be dark alchemy, a precise formula that gave them all their heart\u2019s desires. Hunters who face down Transcendents carry with them tales of a man who took a shotgun blast to his bare chest and kept charging, a woman who could burn a man\u2019s skin with just a touch, and a delusional prophet whose very words were honey. There is <i>something</i> out there that is willing to reward slashers for their bitter deeds, and as long as there is murder in the world, it will <i>always</i> have a supplicant.<br /> <br /> <b>Background</b>: Many serial killers have a superiority complex. They honestly believe that they are above the rest of humanity, that the average man means as much to them as the average cattle. The Transcendent not only follows this ethos, but adheres to it with a steely certainty; he <i>knows</i> for a fact that he is more than mortal.<br /> <br /> While the Transcendent is most often the \u201cevolved\u201d state of a Stranger who has discovered the truth of his Undertaking, it\u2019s possible for a slasher to instantly reach the state of accomplishment in a moment of dreadful revelation. Perhaps he finds a horrible secret of the universe written in a dusty tome, or discovers his bloodline is traced to an ancient clan of monsters. Those members of VASCU who know about the Lucifuge look upon the Children of the Seventh Generation with distrust; when you believe yourself to be a child of Hell, it\u2019s only a matter of degrees until you\u2019re doing the Devil\u2019s will.<br /> <br /> Like the Stranger, the character creation for a Transcendent is flexible and depends greatly on the focus of the rebirth. The man who desires to become a Faustian devil will focus his interests in a different direction than the woman who wishes to embody the wrath of the Furies. Another important factor in creating a Transcendent is that they are, at their very core, malleable. Their Talent lies in adopting the traits of their new self; they can be whatever they want, as long as it fits their ethos.<br /> <br /> <b>Inspirations</b>: Serial Killer X (<i>Condemned: Criminal Origins</i>), Edgar Reese/Azazel (<i>Fallen</i>), The Metal Fetishist (<i>Tetsuo the Iron Man</i>), SID 6.7 (<i>Virtuosity</i>)<br /> <br /> <b>Attribute</b>: Intelligence, Resolve, Dexterity or Stamina<br /> <br /> <b>Undertaking Skills</b>: Academics, Animal Ken, Intimidation, Investigation, Larceny, Medicine, Occult, Streetwise, Survival, Weaponry<br /> <br /> <b>Talent \u2013 Malleable Self</b>: The Transcendent appears mortal, but can call forth his true self at will. Once per scene, the Transcendent can spend a point of Willpower and roll Resolve + Composure. He cannot risk Willpower on this roll, or spend Willpower to increase the roll itself. Once the roll is made, the Transcendent can spend successes on changes to their form:<br /> <br /> -+1 to Skill (1 success per dot)<br /> -+1 to Attribute (3 successes per dot)<br /> -Iron Stamina Merit(1 success per dot)<br /> -Striking Looks Merit (1 success for 2 dots, 2 successes for 4 dots)<br /> -Natural Weaponry (1 success per +1L; 1 extra success to make damage elemental)<br /> -Natural Armor (2 successes per level)<br /> -Healing damage (1 success per level of Bashing, 2 successes per level of Lethal, 4 successes per level of Aggravated)<br /> <br /> These changes <i>must</i> relate to the form they have adopted; the Storyteller has final say on whether or not an adaptation is thematically related.<br /> <br /> <b>Frailty \u2013 Only Human</b>: The Transcendent may believe he has grown beyond the bonds of humanity, but in many ways, he is still fettered to the corpse of his old self. His weakness lies in being reminded that he is still mortal, and his \u201ctrue self\u201d is mere decoration added to human clay. Like with his Talent, the Transcendent\u2019s Frailty is entirely thematic. A white supremacist self-proclaimed <i>ubermensch</i> may find a black hunter has gotten the upper hand in a fist fight, whereas a woman who patterns herself after the Great Whore of Babylon and delights in driving holy men to ruination may find sympathy at the hands of a member of the Long Night.<br /> <br /> When the Transcendent is confronted with evidence of his old self and human failings, the mask cracks instantly. All benefits derived from their Talent vanish automatically, leaving his with just his natural aptitudes. Furthermore, crushing doubt overtakes the Transcendent as he struggles with the knowledge that he isn\u2019t as perfect as he believes; as a result, he takes a -2 penalty to <i>all</i> rolls for the remainder of the scene. Most Transcendents flee from such confrontations, usually isolating themselves until they\u2019ve managed to suppress the crushing realization\u2026 and swear revenge on those who brought forth their flaws.<br /> <br /> <b>VASCU Case Study: Lilith</b><br /> <br /> <i>From the files of anthropologist Michael Ntuze<br /> <br /> I first met Dr. Lillian Carver three years into my fellowship at the Smithsonian, when I was leading a program into the search for \u201cMitochondrial Eve\u201d \u2013 the common ancestor of all humanity. She came to us with a laundry list of accolades: summa cum laude at Georgetown, graduate study at Oxford, a Pell Grant at 25\u2026 she certainly knew the territory. She had spent years on research expeditions in Africa, following the trail of anthropological studies. We did question the fact that her studies had taken her to Nigeria, Sudan, and Zimbabwe during periods of civil unrest and genocide; her only explanation was that she \u201cstudied with the best.\u201d<br /> <br /> From the start, there seemed something\u2026 odd about Dr. Carver. She always seemed withdrawn, and never joined us outside of work. I had known my share of eccentrics during my stay in academia, and merely attributed it to personal quirks. Then I heard stories of the men who turned up in motel rooms on I-495, subjected to extensive surgery while they were still alive. Around this time, I began to notice a change in Dr. Carver \u2013 she seemed more vivacious, more alluring, and even fervid at times.<br /> <br /> When she failed to show up for work for three days, I took one of the slides from her worktable to the police on a whim \u2013 it had come from one of the men on I-495. They came to our lab and found a manifest on her computer, proclaiming herself to be \u201cthe outlier,\u201d \u201cthe betrayed mother of humanity.\u201d The letter was signed, \u201cLilith.\u201d<br /> <br /> Every few months, I receive a new slide from her. I never test it.</i><br /> <br /> <b>The Predator (Ripper)</b><br /> <br /> While most slashers enjoy the hunt and stalking of their prey, for most it\u2019s a means to an end. For the Predator the hunt is the thing. They live for the chase. The kill is almost a letdown, though they realize it\u2019s an inevitable end to the ritual and even while they are taking their victim\u2019s life they are looking forward to the next hunt. They often refer to their victims as \u201cprey\u201d, \u201canimals\u201d, or similar dehumanizing terms. They do this because they truly do not see those they kill as human, merely as outlets for their desires.<br /> <br /> Many Predators share some traits with other undertakings. They are ruthless and violent like the Brute. They feel set aside and above the rest of humanity like the Genius. They even sometimes feel outcast and distant from others like the Freak (though they are rarely ugly or deformed). A few use flattery and seduction to draw their quarry near, much like a Charmer. However, in the end they are Predators, and their whole nature and reason for being revolves around this fact.<br /> <br /> Predators more than any other slasher are likely to take trophies from their victims. For them these mementos allow them to relive the thrill of tracking their victim, tormenting them, and feeling the sense of power and joy as they end their life. Many Predators have signatures weapons and methods they use in their kills. Some even have special hunting grounds set aside.<br /> <br /> Predators are often solitary, though they sometimes band together with other slashers to stage particularly elaborate hunts. Some Predators have even managed to join hunter cells and direct them towards their victims. In some cases these victims are truly guilty of some terrible offense, though Predators have been known to frame a target. A few rare Predators hunt hunters, supernatural creatures, or ever other slashers, considering them the most challenging prey of all.<br /> <br /> <b>Background:</b><br /> <br /> Most Predators begin as hunters, law enforcement, or other professions who specialize in tracking, catching, or killing humans or animals. Others comes from other professions but are active sportsmen in their private lives. A few Predators have no such background, but find themselves driven to hunt and kill because of some deep-seated mental ailment.<br /> <br /> At times a hunter will become a Predator. This happens when a hunter\u2019s mission becomes more about the hunt and the challenge of tracking demons, monsters, and other enemies more than it does about stopping evil or helping people.<br /> <br /> In all cases, the Predator spends time and effort to learn, refine, and perfect the hunt. They may stalk their first victims for days, or even weeks, before they escalate. They tend to refine their art over time, and often their first stalks and kills seem crude and primitive compared to the killer they will become.<br /> <br /> Predators usually have a focus on Physical Attributes and Skills, though they often have high ratings in Wits, Resolve, or Composure to reflect the controlled and superior air so many cultivate. Many have Merits which either help them in attracting prey or dispatching them.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Inspirations: Thomas Burns (Surviving the Game), General Zaraoff (The Most Dangerous Game), Kraven the Hunter (Spider-Man), Aaron Hallum (The Hunted)<br /> <br /> Attributes: Dexterity, Resolve, or Wits<br /> <br /> Undertaking Skills: Animal Ken, Survival, Firearms, Weaponry, Stealth, Crafts, Investigation, Subterfuge</i></b><br /> <br /> <b>Talent- I Have Your Scent</b><br /> A Predator fixates on his target. He learns their abilities, habits, and weaknesses. Once a Predator has picked his target he gains a +1 die bonus to all rolls involving the target, including tracking and killing them. This bonus lasts until the victim is killed or the Predator abandons the hunt. If he does so he must wait at least 24 hours before being able to apply the bonus to new prey. If he kills his prey he suffers no such limitation.<br /> <br /> <b>Frailty- Thrill of the Hunt</b><br /> A Predator cannot simply kill his victim. He must stalk them, wear them down, and then eventually finish them off only when he has demonstrated his superiority. Every victim must be given a \u201cfair chance\u201d to survive. How actually fair this is varies greatly, but at the very least a victim must be given a chance to detect, fight, or otherwise escape before the Predator feels he can truly satisfy his need for sport. The ability of the prey is often a factor here: an ex-marine sniper might be brought down after he fails to spot the Predator when he reveals himself for a mere instant while a suburban housewife might be handed a knife and given a five minute head start.<br /> <br /> <b><i>VASCU Case Study: Orion</i></b><br /> <i>\u201cBorn Edgar Henry Wilson, the killer known as Orion was a ex-Army Ranger who was dishonorably discharged after an incident during the first Gulf War. The file\u2019s sealed and we\u2019re trying to get clearance but you know how that goes. Afterwards it seems Wilson spent some time in Africa as a merc, He even worked as a safari guide before he dropped off the radar a few years back. He recently resurfaced in connection with the Alaskan Bush Murders. Over a period of eighteen months Wilson captured a number of fish and wildlife guides, mostly local Inuits. He then released his victims in remote areas, apparently giving them a knife and a few days rations. Without fail, Wilson hunted and killed all of his victims. His preferred weapon of choice seems to be a hunting crossbow, though many of his victims were struck mortal wounds with some type of long knife or sword.<br /> <br /> Wilson takes his moniker from two factors. First, he is skilled hunter who fancies himself a modern day hero in the Greek sense. Second, and more chilling, he left each of his ten victims in a pattern which when placed on a map approximates the major stars in the constellation Orion.<br /> <br /> Authorities discovered Wilson\u2019s identity but were unable to apprehend. He vanished shortly thereafter and there are no reliable reports of him since. However, the FBI office in Seattle has recently been tracking a number of killings of local police officers. Though preliminary reports are inconclusive, it seems that the location of the first four killings correspond with the belt and sword tip of the Orion constellation. We recommend sending agents to assist local law enforcement and investigate further.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <b>The Beast (Scourge)</b><br /> <br /> A Predator who is completely consumed by the hunt is the Beast. He sees himself not only as the ultimate hunter but the ultimate creature. He is the top of the food chain, the king of all the animals, and the lord of the jungle all rolled into one terrible package. The Beast is in control even when he is being hunted and some even prefer to let their victims play the role of pursuer for a time.<br /> <br /> Beasts are more primal and feral than their Predator counterparts. They can speak and interact with normal humans, but rarely do so except on the most primal levels. Many are cannibals, ingesting their victim\u2019s power with their flesh. Others are creatures of only barely restrained lust and dark desires. Beasts sometimes employ animals in their hunts- abused or twisted companions who are as ruthless and terrible as their masters. They tend to kill more and with increased savagery. Some even take to marking and maiming their foes and allowing them to linger for a time. They don\u2019t do this solely out of sadism, but as a testament to the power and superiority they hold over their victims.<br /> <br /> Most Beasts dwell outside society as much as they can afford. Many are wanderers or hermits, living in cabins in the deep woods or always traveling from one small town to the next. Some do come to the city, seeing it as a jungle of stone and steel in which to stalk and kill.<br /> <br /> Predators often become Beasts after a period of boredom or dissatisfaction with their previous Undertaking. Unlike many slashers, they want to be challenged almost to the point of failure and too much success causes them to seek a new methodology. At this time, the Predator comes to the realization that they cannot be satisfied as they are. As the supreme stalker, the perfect killer, there is nothing left to do but evolve. With this realization another Beast is born.<br /> <br /> Despite their near-feral nature, some Beasts can blend in with normal humans- at least for a time. They might join hunting parties or camping excursions, playing the role of the friendly guide or even the clueless newbie. Eventually, away from civilization, they will drop this guise and begin to prey upon their companions. Some Beasts even delight in dragging out their ruse by isolating and killing victims and then calling the others to see what some \u201cwild animal\u201d or \u201ccrazy killer\u201d has done.<br /> <br /> Beasts often embrace primitive weaponry and fighting techniques. In part this is an extension of the ever-increasing challenge they sought as Predators. However, it is also part of the supernatural aspect of their new Undertaking. They are just as much savage animal as rational man- balancing cunning and primal ferocity with ingenuity and advanced reasoning.<br /> <br /> <b>Background: </b><br /> <br /> Most Beasts begin as Predators. However, the occasional killer becomes the Beast immediately. These slashers usually have some special connection to the wilderness or animal kingdom. A feral child might become the Beast if they are driven to prey on humans for food or sport. A desperate hunter might embrace the Undertaking to justify the horrible things he did while trapped in the wild.<br /> <br /> Even more so than Predators, Beasts favor Physical Traits and Skills. Though it is not a favored Attribute their Strength tends to be noticeably higher than their Predator brethren. Mental Attributes and Skills are often lacking though Beasts are rarely stupid. Social Attributes and Skills tend to be focused on Intimidation, Animal Ken, and Presence. Beasts who prefer to hide among their prey also often have some aptitude with Manipulation and Subterfuge. Most Beasts possess Atavism or the Fighting Style: Frenzied Assault Merits. Many possess both.<br /> <br /> <b>Inspirations: Steve (Shoot to Kill), Kraven the Hunter (Kraven\u2019s Last Hunt, an excellent example of the progression from Predator to Beast), Jean-Francois de Morangias (Brotherhood of the Wolf/Le Pacts des Loups),<br /> <br /> Attributes: Dexterity, Resolve, or Wits<br /> <br /> Undertaking Skills: Animal Ken, Survival, Firearms, Weaponry, Stealth, Crafts, Investigation, Subterfuge</b><br /> <br /> <b>Talent- Top of the Food Chain</b><br /> <br /> Those who encounter a Beast feel the full effect of their animalistic nature. The Beast adds +1 bonus die to all attempts to cow, intimidate, or frighten. In addition, the nature of the Beast seems to exert some primitive control over the instincts of its prey. When successfully intimidating a target, the Beast can select whether the basic response follows a \u201cfight\u201d or a \u201cflight\u201d pattern. They cannot exert fine control over their target, but they can choose the basic reaction. Thus a Beast could decide that a person will engage in a fight response, but they cannot control if that person throws a punch at them, tries to go for a weapon and attack them, or any other aggressive action. Beasts use this Trait to lure their prey or to drive them from places of safety. Some even use this Trait to make others seem like the aggressor or a coward to others, which is useful to remove obstacles on their hunts.<br /> <br /> Three circumstances increase the bonuses from this Trait. First, this bonus increases to +2 dice with animals, as they can sense the threat of the Beast with greater ease. Second, this same bonus also applies to any prey chosen by the Predator Trait I Have Your Scent. Third, when the Beast spends a Willpower to augment die rolls using this Trait he gains a 9 again on the roll in addition to the normal Willpower bonus.<br /> <br /> <b>Fraility- Law of the Jungle</b><br /> <br /> Beasts are prisoners of their instincts and their own self. They must act in accordance with their status as supreme Beast and lord of the wild or be driven to distraction. They must answer challenges, confront those who violate their territory or lairs, and otherwise behave in ways commonly associated with a territorial, aggressive, and dangerous animal. They need not be immediate or foolish in this behavior- a Beast could decide to stalk a cop who insulted and called them out on the news to a remote locale and confront them. However, they must act accordingly or take substantial steps towards doing so. If they seek to avoid this behavior they suffer a -3 penalty on all actions due to the distraction, anger, and shame of denying their natures. This penalty disappears when the Beast engages in the appropriate behavior he has been avoiding.<br /> <br /> A side effect of this Frailty is noteworthy if rarely a factor. Anyone who defeats the Beast soundly in combat or otherwise proves his superiority gains a level of deference and respect. This causes the Beast to generally want to avoid this person and if forced to confront them they suffer the -3 dice penalty to combat rolls to attack this character (they still defend normally). This situation only comes into play when another character bests the Beast in a \u201cfair\u201d one on one confrontation where there is no doubt of the victor. Note this situation is exceedingly rare, since most Beast swill fight to the bitter end rather than admit they can be bested and few hunters or would be victims who gain the upper hand are inclined to spare the slasher if they get the better of him.<br /> <br /> <b><i>VASCU Case File: The Jaguar Man</i></b><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cWe still don\u2019t have a real name on this perp yet. We\u2019re calling him the Jaguar Man because of our one reliable sighting so far.<br /> <br /> The eyewitness report had this guy running around in nothing but spotted pelts and some sort of tribal jewelry. Our experts have identified this garb as a variation of the Aztec warriors the ocelotl, or Jaguar Warriors. They think the killer identifies with these ancient soldiers and their culture, or at least some aspects of it such as blood sacrifice and ritual murder. Despite the connection to Aztecs in methodology, our experts suspect the killer isn\u2019t of Mesoamerican descent. I\u2019m a bit unclear on all the reasoning myself, but eyewitness reports do describe the killer as having light skin and hair.<br /> <br /> The Jaguar Man primary murder weapons are what forensics thinks are some sort of blades made of obsidian. Wounds on the bodies of the victims seem to suggest at least two different implements were used. Whether these are some stolen museum relic or tools the killer made himself is unclear. The killer uses these weapons to wound his victim to the point of incapacitation. He extracts the heart of his victims while they are still alive. He then leaves the body where it fell and takes the heart. We don\u2019t know what he does with the hearts he takes.<br /> <br /> The Jaguar Man doesn\u2019t seem to be tied down to one particular territory. He operates in an area for a time and then migrates to a new location. He mostly stays around the American Southwest and Northern Mexico, though we have reports of possible killings in Seattle, Chicago, and Philadelphia. To date, he is suspected in the killings of at least sixty victims in the United States alone. We\u2019re still waiting on accurate data from the Mexican authorities but we suspect to at least double that number.<br /> <br /> Attached Memo: Now you\u2019d think we\u2019d able to catch a crazy guy in a loincloth using stone knives but let\u2019s not get cocky here. We\u2019ve already lost two agents on this case.\u201d</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":483,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","user":"Flyboy254","date":". 08-26-2017, 03:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T13:16:06-07:00","id":1134231,"title":"","content":"<b>Chameleon</b><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cI\u2019ve just got one of those faces.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> Robin Dunbar proposed a concept that the human brain only has the cognitive ability to maintain roughly 150 stable relationships. While some have criticized it the theory on the basis that this ignores the many social connections necessary to build up human civilization at all, no one can deny that they only have so many many people they can remember and care enough about to interact with on a regular basis. Everyone else is a face in the crowd, shifting through the observer\u2019s life with hardly a thought about the anonymous beings walking about around them.<br /> <br /> What happens to the people who manage through no fault of their own to slip between the cracks of everyone else\u2019s sphere? Who somehow go nearly their entire lives without close friends or romances? Some just go on with their lives, quietly living as they do and suffering the loneliness that aches at their hearts. Others feel enraged by this, angered that their lives are somehow unseen and unheard by those around them, and they are willing to do anything it takes to be noticed by those around them.<br /> <br /> A Chameleon is aptly named, able to slip in and out of any location simply by blending into the background. Their targets may think they were nothing more than an accidental bump into a shoulder on the subway, a passing nod to a stranger on the street, a shopkeepers smile to a customer before he departs never to be seen again, but to the Chameleon these run ins are the closest they have to real human contact, and it's not enough. To a Chameleon murder is a shout into the world: &quot;I exist! I will no longer be ignored!&quot;. Some Chamelions kill because they feel slighted in some way by their victims. They seek revenge against the waiter who overlooked them for hours, or anyone who resembles the pretty girl at school who never knew he existed. Other Chameleons target a circle of friends one by one until they can't help but spend every waking moment worrying about their mysterious asailent. Or they choose targets, weapons, and a modus operandi to splash a larger than life persona across the front pages, a persona nobody would ever connect with the quiet man collecting the trash.<br /> <br /> In either case, the chameleon is a patient predator. They slowly move themselves into the lives of those they follow without ever being noticed. They track their targets, trailing them to and from work, about their lives, and inevitably either growing envious of the fact that other people care about them, or of the others who spend time with the person who shows them the attention they so sorely lack. Wheather a quick kill or an elabourate statement, a Chameleon's murder can be as invisible as themselves, with every angle scouted and checked to make sure it's free of witnesses and evidence.<br /> <br /> What makes a Chameleon dangerous is that they easily blend in anywhere. They\u2019re the \u201ckiller cop\u201d, putting flashing lights on the roof of his car and buying a prop badge to lure out the unsuspecting motorists he kidnaps and kills. He\u2019s a lowly janitor, fired months ago but still coming in to work because no one cares enough to check his badge to see it\u2019s out of date. All he is, is a face in the crowd that can\u2019t be seen. It\u2019s not that he\u2019s a master of disguise, in fact many of the chameleons captured barely have what could be considered a \u201cwardrobe\u201d at all. Their \u201cgift\u201d is that the rest of the world simply considers them invisible.<br /> <br /> <b>Background:</b> Not many Hunters wind up as Chameleons, they\u2019re ingratiated too greatly with their cells to be unnoticed in the same way these poor souls are. But many Hunters have allies and informants outside the camandarie of the cell, when the heat is on these inside men can be left alone and isolated. Bereft of both social contact and the safety of the mundane world they sometimes find that when they finally escape and cut their ties to the supernatural they no longer belong among normal people, and they will do anything to seize a place.<br /> <br /> Most people who wind up becoming Chameleons were never part of the vigil. They were ordinary, perhaps too ordinary, and ignored by everyone around them. They lived lives of quiet resentment or seething bitterness that grew and grew until the day they snapped. Others were ordinary and sociable people until some traumatic incident caused them to retreat from the world, or the world to retreat from them rather than confront the uncomfortable truths behind the crime. They tried and failed to return to the world, and then they decided they'd try more drastic measures to be seen again. These Chameleons inevitably work their backstory into their Undertaking and the murders they commit.<br /> <br /> Chameleons tend to have very high Composure, with no human outlet for their emotions they have gotten very good at bottling up their feelings. Their skill in Subterfuge is also usually decent, they're not invisible so knowing how to stay in charachter when the foreman asks the nearest janitor to handle a task is vital, but few Chameleons master more than the basics of Subterfuge, they just don't have the opportunity to practice the more subtle intricacies of social interaction. Most other social abilities are non-existent, though a few Chameleons can from a nobody to a blazing Presence with terrifying Intimidation the moment they have a victim at their mercy.<br /> <br /> Stealth is usually high, despite the fact Chameleons can rely on their Talent over more mundane tricks Stealth comes naturally to them. Many Chameleons have managed to disappear into a crowd or the shadows after VASCU agents have blown their cover. Crafts and Survival are also common skills, being invisible to society often means working menial jobs and taking care of yourself. Mental Skills and Attributes can be surprisingly high, society finds it easier to overlook the quiet kid behaving himself in the library than outgoing or misbehaving kids, and an empty social calender leaves plenty of time for study and mental pursuits.<br /> <br /> <b>Inspirations:</b> Zartan (G.I. Joe: Rise of Cobra); False Face (Batman); Carlos the Jackal (Day of the Jackal); Jean-Baptiste Grenouille (Perfume)<br /> <br /> <b>Attribute:</b> Composure<br /> <br /> <b>Undertaking Skill:</b> Academics, Computer, Investigation, Crafts, Larceny, Stealth, Survival, Weaponry<br /> <br /> <b>Talent: </b>A Thousand Masks<br /> <br /> <b>Frailty:</b> Telltale Sign<br /> <br /> <i>VASCU Case File: \u201cThe Newsboy\u201d</i><br /> <br /> <i>Notes from Det. Frank Bianchi, NYPD</i><br /> <br /> <i>Uniforms found another last night. Young girl, couldn\u2019t be older than 22, no ID just like the others. Stabbed multiple times, left to bleed out, posed to look like she was homeless. Lucky for us, the spot where she was left actually belonged to a bum.</i><br /> <br /> <i>The captain\u2019s getting on my ass about this one, but we don\u2019t fucking know where to start. Every witness doesn\u2019t remember anyone really standing out. They don\u2019t remember anyone talking to the victim, her friends don\u2019t mention anyone following her the past few days, it\u2019s all turning up empty.</i><br /> <br /> <i>The only connection between the victims is that they all stopped at the same news stand to grab a magazine or newspaper. Owner said he didn\u2019t see anything suspicious either, no one tracking them or acting like they were too interested.</i><br /> <br /> <i>Christ, they\u2019re gonna have my shield if we don\u2019t figure this one out soon. I\u2019ll go back to the stand today, see if the guy might\u2019ve remembered something since the last time we spoke.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T13:41:07-07:00","id":1134240,"title":"","content":"Here's the rough idea for the Boogeyman.<br /> <br /> <b>Boogeyman</b><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cDon\u2019t you recognize me?\u201d</i><br /> <br /> Some people go beyond simply being ignored or missed by society. A few realize that they might as well be invisible to anyone and everyone. They can slip past cameras, avoid the best lookouts, mock any attempts by guards to stop them in their tracks. Whether through a preternatural skill at disguise or being able to vanish into thin air, they are the literal stuff of nightmares: A Boogeyman.<br /> <br /> Boogeyman slashers have gone beyond caring about being noticed by the wider world. They tried that, and it didn\u2019t work. Now their only goal is terror, being the shadows in the night that mothers tell stories about to keep their children behaved in their beds. They\u2019re the things that teenagers in lovers lanes across the country whisper as the reason they don\u2019t want to be out after dark. The Boogeyman is practically a force of nature more than a man, choosing when to be seen and when to vanish after the kill.<br /> <br /> Finding a Boogeyman is extremely rare, and most hunters would consider the prospect of going after such a killer terrifying to consider. It\u2019s one thing to face down a killer who you\u2019d have trouble noticing, and a utterly terrifying concept of facing down a human being that you can\u2019t see coming until it\u2019s too late. Even other slashers find a Boogeyman terrifying, since even they aren\u2019t safe from the invisible killer lurking in their own hunting grounds. Once a Boogeyman decides he\u2019s taken claim over an area, no one is truly safe until someone puts him down, a feat easier said than done.<br /> <br /> What is a Boogeyman then? Are they still truly human? Some of their abilities might seem like the gift to shapeshift, but others claim that a Boogeyman is actually able to phase in and out of physical form, almost like a ghost. Some hunters have tried to capture them, only for their targets to apparently walk straight through the walls holding them and continue their murders. Few records on them even exist for the conspiracies, but all share a common theme.<br /> <br /> To the rest of the world, they might as well not exist.<br /> <br /> <b>Background:</b> No one just <i>becomes</i> a Boogeyman, at least not often. Something just happens to chameleons who realize that even their murders aren\u2019t bringing them any closer to the rest of humanity. What they become attached to is murder, the only part of their lives that still brings them close to other human beings. How they leave humanity behind isn\u2019t yet known, but they simply seem to phase out compared to other humans.<br /> <br /> Boogeyman can be said to actively exist in a state of something close to what occultists call \u201cTwilight\u201d. They can seemingly slip in and out of locked rooms, avoid the gaze of watchful guards and police, appear and vanish at will to further torment their victims. Being part of humanity is fully off the table. The Boogeyman <i>thrives</i> off the terror of their kills, and makes a point to never let them feel alone until the light leaves their eyes.<br /> <br /> <b>Inspiration:</b> Nathaniel Teager (The X-Files);<br /> <br /> <b>Talent: Not Part of Your World</b><br /> <br /> <b>Frailty: Lingering Humanity</b><br /> <br /> <i>VASCU Case File: \u201cJohnny J. Johnson\u201d<br /> Note: The attached note is a local children's rhyme from outside Providence. I think we finally have a name.</i><br /> <br /> <i>Johnny J. Johnson</i><br /> <i>Went up to Boston</i><br /> <i>Cause somebody stole his hen</i><br /> <br /> <i>Johnny J. Johnson</i><br /> <i>Went up to Boston</i><br /> <i>Never came back again</i><br /> <br /> <i>Johnny J. Johnson</i><br /> <i>Never came home</i><br /> <i>Now hide inside, it\u2019s true</i><br /> <br /> <i>Cause if Johnny J. Johnson</i><br /> <i>Think\u2019s you\u2019re the thief</i><br /> <i>Then he\u2019s coming after you!</i><br /> <br /> <i>He\u2019ll move through locked doors</i><br /> <i>A window\u2019s no chore</i><br /> <i>He\u2019ll come down your chimney flue</i><br /> <br /> <i>Yes Johnny J. Johnson</i><br /> <i>Who went up to Boston</i><br /> <i>Will be coming after you!</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":483,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","user":"Flyboy254","date":". 08-26-2017, 07:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T18:52:09-07:00","id":1134316,"title":"","content":"Okay, here's what I've got for the intro right now. Consider the lists incomplete until you guys figure on what groups do and don't count as cults.<br /> <br /> <b>Introduction</b><br /> <br /> <b>The Candle At Both Ends</b><br /> <br /> The Vigil is massive in scope. Vampires have their small fiefdoms, werewolves have their territories, fairies their freeholds. Hunters are everywhere you can look. From the frozen wastes of Ny-\u00c5lesund in Svalbard to the scordhing heat of Stovepipe Wells, California, there are hunters who know that the Vigil is a lifelong commitment. The only way out is in a box, one way or the other.<br /> <br /> It takes many forms. The Vigil is a cell of street bums in London taking the fight to a vampire that was trying to suck a woman dry. It\u2019s a ship\u2019s captain telling the crew to ram the monster rising from the waters in front of them, glad he planned the route for just the right time. It can be seen in lone cells standing up to powerful inquisitors to protect innocent witches from being tortured, and in criminal enterprises running protection rackets to keep the monsters in line. There is no \u201ctypical\u201d Vigil, any more than there\u2019s a \u201ctypical\u201d hunter.<br /> <br /> Compacts rise from ancient ages to carry on their duties. Conspiracies are birthed in the modern age as fellowships unite against the darkness. Cults and cabals tread a fine line between savior and sinner, as the Vigil grows and evolves with time. The only constant is the Vigil itself.<br /> <br /> <b>Light Up the World</b> serves as a further expansion of the concept of the Vigil, from fresh-faced conspiracies to salty compacts to dark cabals and vile cults.<br /> <br /> <b>Chapter 1: Compacts</b> explores several new compacts introduced.<ul><li><b>The DiFillipo Family:</b> American <i>mafioso </i>who find that the Vigil is just good business.</li> <li><b>Bureau de Circonstances Extraordinaire:</b> France\u2019s governmental hunters who hide the dark secrets of their pasts deeply within their halls.</li> <li><b>The Final Girl\u2019s Club:</b> Survivors of slasher attacks who banded together to protect others from the predations of others.</li> <li><b>The Icelos Institute:</b> Psychotherapists and counselors concerned with the supernatural effects on people\u2019s minds.</li> <li><b>The Reality Hackers:</b> Computer experts and savants who believe they\u2019ve found the source code to reality itself.</li> <li><b>Schutzegruppe 14:</b> Germany\u2019s occult experts, purposefully divided to prevent evil from rearing up again.</li> <li><b>P\u0103zitors: </b>Eastern European clergy who survived under communism to carry on their holy fight.</li> <li><b>The Brotherhood of All Worlds:</b> Leftovers of the Summer of Love who believe that the world can be saved with good vibes all around.</li> <li><b>The Parole Gang:</b> Ex-cons and parolees who believe they must continue to repay their debt to society.</li> <li><b>Soci\u00e9t\u00e9 d\u2019Had\u00e8s:</b> Parisian explorers of the secret routes that lead to the Underworld.</li> <li><b>Llannerch Athrawon:</b> Welsh keepers of mythic traditions attempting to channel dangerous heroes on a more righteous path.</li> <li><b>SRO:</b> An insurance company specializing in the risks presented by the Vigil.</li> <li><b>MI18:</b> England\u2019s agents involved in policing the world\u2019s super-scientific risks.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>Chapter 2: Conspiracies</b> looks into the wider world of the conspiracies that see themselves at the top of the Vigil\u2019s food chain.<ul><li><b>Project: AMMUT:</b> A secret United Nations force targeting the long-undead remnants of mankind\u2019s dark past.</li> <li><b>Hotel Mascaron:</b> Anti-fairy spies and agents working to save mankind from eternal servitude.</li> <li><b>The Athenic Church:</b> Worshippers of the Greek goddess of wisdom that consider it their mission to preserve their faith.</li> <li><b>The Disillusioned:</b> Remnants of fallen power who take it on themselves to right past wrongs.</li> <li><b>Raziel, Ltd.: </b>Israeli weapons manufacturers that believe it is a holy duty to hunt down that which is born from Lilith</li> <li><b>The Brotherhood Prizrakov:</b> Divers into the Earth and far below it, conquering the underworlds for profit.</li> <li><b>The Shih:</b> Chinese mystics who seek balance in all things, even the Vigil.</li> <li><b>KSI 21:</b> The reinvigorated ghost of a Soviet program using spectral agents to gather information on Russia\u2019s enemies.</li> <li><b>The Carpenters:</b> American civil servants bound together by the shared interest in keeping America stable and secure.</li> <li><b>Haans-Chowdhury Productions:</b> An Indian corporation that turns ancient secrets into modern weapons against the darkness.</li> <li><b>Hakollel shen Hamerkava:</b> Jewish mystics who have found the ability to create their own protectors.</li> <li><b>Aki Ten:</b> Japanese practitioners of <i>Onmyodo</i>, using spirits are their vassals</li> </ul><br /> <b>Chapter 3: Cults and Cabals</b> dives deep into organizations that tread a fine line in the Vigil\u2019s candlelight. Are they hunters to seek out, or cults to drive away?<ul><li><b>Cult of Moloch:</b> Cultists who believe that no power can be gained without appropriate sacrifice.</li> <li><b>The Fire-Touched:</b> Masochistic cultists who believe they can gain power through their mystic brands.</li> <li><b>The Knights-Errant:</b> Questing seekers looking for what some claim is the ultimate artifact.</li> <li><b>Bastet\u2019s Beloved: </b>Worshippers of the Egyptian goddess of cats, who returns their worship with protection.</li> <li><b>Cage of Shadows:</b> Followers of Lilith, believing that it is their duty to elevate their Mother to rule over Earth.</li> <li><b>Bone Collectors:</b> Scavengers of the Vigil, picking up the trash left behind by the fighting between hunters and monsters.</li> <li><b>Heirs of the Crown: </b>Demon-summoners, seeking the power of the unholy for their own gain.</li> </ul><br /> <b>Chapter 4: Tools and Tricks</b> looks at new endowments, professions, and slasher undertakings created to expand the Vigil even wider.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T00:26:04-07:00","id":1134384,"title":"","content":"I believe the Order of the Sheltered Spire and the Athenic Church are gonna be moved into Chapter 3 since they were pulled from the Cults fandbook. Do we have a working definition of &quot;Convention&quot; yet because I never found one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T00:29:44-07:00","id":1134385,"title":"","content":"That's a negative on my end. Kings?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T00:39:48-07:00","id":1134387,"title":"","content":"You asked the right person, I came up with the term <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Conventions are groups that aren't organisations in any shape or form, but a collection of individuals who due to some (usually supernatural) reason share a vigil. So for example Bastet's Beloved: They don't go out and recruit vets and zoo keepers then teach them cat magic from ye olde dusty tome of lore. Bastet herself is responsible for people around the world developing supernatural powers; and because she has specific criteria the people who get her powers share common traits; so apart from the fact most Beloved never meet another of their kind, they resemble a Compact.<br /> <br /> I also came up with Circle/Cabal/Covenant for cults; but I was thinking they might work better for groups like The Athenic Church who don't fit the Hunter ideal of humans striking back against monsters (they take direct orders from a Goddess on a daily basis) but in terms of goals, behaviour, and integration into regular society resemble Hunters far more than monsters<ul><li><b>MI18:</b> England\u2019s agents involved in policing the world\u2019s super-scientific risks (BTW, they're a Conspiracy)</li> <li><b>KSI 21:</b> The reinvigorated ghost of a Soviet program using spectral agents to gather information on Russia\u2019s enemies.</li> <li><b>Llannerch Athrawon:</b> Masters of illusion and psychology who channel dangerous heroes on a more righteous path. (they're not actually Welsh; they're of no specific origin. The Welsh name is part of the pretending to be Merlin schtick)</li> <li><b>The Athenic Church:</b> Worshippers of the Roman goddess of wisdom sent forth to spread their faith.</li> <li><b>Hakollel shen Hamerkava:</b> Jewish mystics who wield and protect the secret names of God.</li> <li><b>Bastet\u2019s Beloved: </b>Cat lovers blessed and protected by Bastet.</li> <li><b>The Barkers Street Irregulars: </b>Genius detectives struggling with personality disorders.</li> <li><b>The Reality Hackers: </b> Computer scientists and theologians who debug errors in reality.</li> <li><b>The Order of St. Anthony: </b>Battered but not broken by the Soviets, the Eastern Orthodox Church stands against the darkness.</li> <li><b>The Staff of Janus: </b>The guardians at the gate between Earth and elsewhere.</li> <li><b>Ride to Damascus: </b>Master storytellers re-imagining the old tales of Beasts and Heroes.</li> <li><b>Hearth of Hestia: </b>Housewives who protect their homes through love for their family.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-27-2017, 03:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T00:46:59-07:00","id":1134388,"title":"","content":"Ahh. Interesting. I think I caught on to the fact that Conventions were looser in structure but I think my brain immediately went to &quot;they are essentially an ideological movement but for Hunters&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T02:44:42-07:00","id":1134411,"title":"","content":"Hi! Sorry I haven't replied for a while- I was on a vacation, and lacked any access to a computer, so I couldn't reply to the thread. In the meanwhile, I have worked upon a list of groups I wrote that I would like to see in the supplement (in addition to the ones which already show up in Flyboy's list)-<br /> <br /> <u><b>Compacts</b></u><br /> <b>Sabaoth-</b> a mercenary company which use alchemy to transform themselves into angels and hunt down those hated by Heaven<br /> <b>Silver Syndicate</b>- an investments company with ties in the underworld which use spirit magic to influence the stock market<br /> <b>Maw of the River-</b> a secret order of assassin which devour relics and their curses to bring them back to the River of Life<br /> <b>Maagal HaBaal VeHaAshera-</b> a compact of artists which was formed upon the foundations of a long lost conspiracy of idol makers<br /> <b>Theater of Tragedies-</b> brothel of cross dressers which use false identities to make pacts with demons and cheat their way out (may also be considered a Cult)<br /> <b>Nimrod Movement-</b> political movement which rebel against God and take over His angels to bring him down<br /> <br /> <b><u>Conspiracies</u></b><br /> <b>Zmei Initiative-</b> psychic Russian mercenaries which can track their origin back to the cold war<br /> <b>Schrlach Spinnwebe-</b> network of blood doll traders which use a strange blood magic to enslave the vampires who drink from them<br /> <b>Nibiru-</b> an ancient conspiracy which maintains the bindings of terrible old gods and seal new ones<br /> <b>Museum Secretorum-</b> collectors of strange phenomena and creatures which lock witches in amber to gain their powers<br /> <b>Al Rih al Asuad-</b> descendants of a Mesopotamian wind demons which fight against the spawn of Lamashtu<br /> <b>R.A.M-</b> an Israeli secret service which works to secure dangerous relics and infiltrate the cults which gather them<br /> <b>Ebony Fangs-</b> hunters of the dead which force upon them the Old Laws of the Underworld, which also slowly kill their organization (may be put in the Compact or Cult section if you prefer)<br /> <b>Mori Kage-</b> a clan of ninjas which are bound by pledge with the yokai to bring them back their escaped yosei<br /> <b>Orchestra Fatalibus-</b> musicians which were united during the French Revolution to sing a new fate against the one of the Fae (may be treated as a Compact of you think it is better)<br /> <b>Benei Topheth-</b> children which survived the dread Rite of Moloch and now hunt those who abuse the life of others for personal gain<br /> <b>Yam VeNahar Factories-</b> an Israeli chemical company which harvest other worlds and the souls of legendary beasts for resources<br /> <b>Navio de Tolos-</b> dream pirates which sail the Primordial Dream in search for freedom and adventure<br /> <br /> <b><u>Cults and Cabals</u></b><br /> <b>Pythian Oracles-</b> prophets and diviners which are willing to kill in order to create a better future (Cabal)<br /> <b>Tartarus Enterprise-</b> a cancer conspiracy which works with and defends monsters to create wonders of technology (Cult? I think they are the only Cancer Conspiracy out there, which it is kinda its own thing)<br /> <b>Los Inocentes-</b> spanish cabal of slashers which hunt heretics in God's name, which may or may not still exist. (Cabal)<br /> <b>Ashen Collective</b>- alchemists which seek for a way to harvest the human soul and use both humans and prometheans as test subjects (Cabal)<br /> <b>Order of the Nameless-</b> cult which summons and binds terrible demons from the Void in an attempt to one day take over it (Cult)<br /> <b>Temple of Silence-</b> servants of a long lost goddess which seek to bring eternal sleep to the Nameless Empire (Cult, need to revise their Endowments)<br /> <b>Pomegranate Deme-</b> collectors of antiques, fetter and memorabilia which practice orphic rites to bind the dead to their service (Cult)<br /> <br /> and groups which may be cool if they could show up, but could be cut out for wordcount reasons-<br /> <br /> <b>Apollonian Brotherhood</b>- a cult which worships Apollo the Sun God as an example of excellence (Cult)<br /> <b>Nemontemi-</b> aztec lineage of starry eyed children which now hunts the gods they once worshiped (Conspiracy)<br /> <b>Church of the Blood Moon-</b> an heretic sect which use mystical songs to reveal and lure wolf shaped demons (Conspiracy/Cult)<br /> <b>E.V.E Institution-</b> scientific research facility which tries to evolve humanity to the next level, with the unwanted consequences of making them murderous monsters (Cabal)<br /> <b>Avici Sutra-</b> a reincarnating order of asuras which fight demons in order to escape the cycle of suffering (Conspiracy)<br /> <b>Eye of Heaven-</b> self proclaimed kingmakers which infiltrate cults in order to manipulate mummies in Heaven's name (Conspiracy)<br /> <b>Garden of Hesperides-</b> old cult of healers which enter the Hedge to collect the herbs they need for their medicines (Cult)<br /> <b>A.S.T.R.A.L-</b> religious order turned data company which seeks to control the information flow to regulate Awakenings and transplant living magic to their flesh (Conspiracy)<br /> <br /> Notice that while writing most of my organizations I have never actually set their tier and definition, as I thought it is better for the individual storyteller to make that up. You may see the division above as the &quot;official&quot; one. Once it would be decided which groups are going to be included in the supplement, I'll start finishing the missing sections of those organizations.<br /> <br /> Also, I just want to correct Raziel's line description- they don't have have a direct connection to Lilith, as she is only one of the stories showing up in the Book of Raziel the Angel. They hunt all monsters, not only vampires (in fact, they have more interest in God Machine related phenomena).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 08-27-2017, 07:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T02:48:40-07:00","id":1134414,"title":"","content":"LostLight you have always been a prolific and refreshing treasure round dese parts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T04:21:32-07:00","id":1134433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1127469-fan-group-pdf?p=1133534#post1133534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <b>Master (Scourge)</b><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>while I do think the writeup and concept are really good (good enough to make me nightmares about it), I think the writeup may gain a lot from toning down a little the dog metaphor- while it is creepy and is really good for an example slasher, when the whole writeup is based around it it kinda feels limiting- as if all the Masters in the world use exactly that terminology for their targets and limits things like a Master which use her followers as literal chess pieces (seeing them as &quot;pawns&quot;), parts of a metaphorical machine (&quot;that cog needs to be replaced&quot;), pieces of arts (having a full museum of &quot;beautiful things&quot; which they &quot;found&quot; or &quot;made&quot;) or any other kind of obsessive need for control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T06:37:48-07:00","id":1134447,"title":"","content":"Looking at the Undertakings you posted yesterday Flyboy really makes me want to go through and rework their Talents. Most of them are far too week, you couldn't base an entire strategy around them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T08:00:34-07:00","id":1134469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1127469-fan-group-pdf?p=1134433#post1134433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">while I do think the writeup and concept are really good (good enough to make me nightmares about it), I think the writeup may gain a lot from toning down a little the dog metaphor- while it is creepy and is really good for an example slasher, when the whole writeup is based around it it kinda feels limiting- as if all the Masters in the world use exactly that terminology for their targets and limits things like a Master which use her followers as literal chess pieces (seeing them as &quot;pawns&quot;), parts of a metaphorical machine (&quot;that cog needs to be replaced&quot;), pieces of arts (having a full museum of &quot;beautiful things&quot; which they &quot;found&quot; or &quot;made&quot;) or any other kind of obsessive need for control.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Hmm, I can do an alternate Scourge based on the &quot;art&quot;/control idea. Something like a Collector. While a Minder attempts to raise their victims in a deluded attempt to make them better and (presumably) leaving to make the world a &quot;better place&quot;, Collectors are solely selfish and have no desire to really protect or rear their victims; instead, Collectors are more interested in developing their collection, leaving their victims in a state of pure helplessness because that is the ultimate control. Their MO is lobotomizing their victims or otherwise looking for individuals who are more-or-less incapable of fighting back or objecting (coma patients for example). What they do is effectively playing with dolls that they have made. <br /> <br /> Talent...If I don't use a pastiche of the Master's The Hand that Feeds You, it'll probably be something like staging the bodies of their victims in such a way that it affects the viewers in an extreme way, even when the Collector cannot feasibly move them. They assist the Collector as if they were providing the Collector teamwork. They can also act as secondary actors for any Tactic the Collector uses. This doesn't mean that his victims are able to act on their own; if the Collector is otherwise incapacitated or incarcerated, their victims cannot drag the body or pick the lock by themselves, the Collector must initiate and the victims provide teamwork.<br /> <br /> The Frailty would most-likely be some sort of targeting tick; Collectors have a specific theme in their mind when they start their collection. One may want to turn their victim into dolls or playmates while another wants to recreate a family dinner. One may take to art and prefer to position their victim's body as if they were part of a painting or sculpture. Collectors are affected by the Fugue Persistent Condition with the trigger being either victims that fit into the theme the Collector desires or situations that invoke the themes. The effect of failing a Resolve + Composure roll for Fugue persists until the Collector is away from the situation or until the Collector or the trigger are attacked, otherwise they will remain in a daze observing the object of their delusions. They also value the safety of their collection over their own well-being for the most part, becoming severely enraged when their collection is tampered with, whether by the victims themselves or a third party.<br /> <br /> And for Influences, that would make Doctor X from The Cat Lady a dead ringer as well as Professor Henry Jarrod from House of Wax and possibly Sander Cohen from Bioshock.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T08:59:37-07:00","id":1134485,"title":"","content":"Just got back from Vacation with my new edits from the printouts. Are we still using the old Google Doc, or is there a new place I should put these writeup edit","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pers