theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T12:24:34-07:00","id":1134556,"title":"","content":"Right now, I've been adding some Endowments to the Endowment folder. Right now, it's mainly additions to pre-existing Conspiracies. Should I also add the new Endowments from new Organizations as well or should I keep them with their organization?<br /> <br /> Also, King, because we are adding sections about Cults, do you believe we should transfer some parts of the Cult handbook into the fanbook?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T12:26:11-07:00","id":1134557,"title":"","content":"Which parts did you have in mind?<br /> <br /> If we're doing endowments I'm interested in suggestions for the Staff of Janus, I don't think their sacraments really worked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T12:30:20-07:00","id":1134562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1127469-fan-group-pdf?p=1134557#post1134557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which parts did you have in mind?<br /> <br /> If we're doing endowments I'm interested in suggestions for the Staff of Janus, I don't think their sacraments really worked.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> For the most part, I figure that lifting the Endowments would be a good start as it's one of the more hard, mechanical sections of the book.<br /> <br /> As for some flavor, we could probably include a section dictating what a Circle, Cabal, and Convention is and maybe some of the Cult-building rules?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T12:33:25-07:00","id":1134564,"title":"","content":"The Cult-building rules were designed to also be compact/conspiracy building rules, so maybe generalise them. But feel free to lift all of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T12:36:06-07:00","id":1134566,"title":"","content":"I had some rough outlines for several compact endowments for Barrett Commission, Bear Lodge, and others. I'll post them here when I find them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T12:39:31-07:00","id":1134571,"title":"","content":"Which reminds me, should look into LostLight's versions of Endowments for Compacts as well. We also have some alternate Endowments in general (one of the big ones being Gospels for MM). Gonna add that one soon. Chapter 4 is building up to be respectably chunky.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T12:50:59-07:00","id":1134580,"title":"","content":"So long as we put out a quality product, it can be the size of the Western canon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T13:55:58-07:00","id":1134598,"title":"","content":"I based these on the 1E rules and not my own GMC update.<br /> <br /> <b>Splinter </b>(Ripper)<br /> <br /> Talent: Two-Faced: Splits have two distinct personalities and appearances, which are completely irreconcilable. They do not think the same way or have any of the same habits. Their abilities, virtues, and vices are the same, but they manifest in different ways. When investigating a Splinter, a regular Success on a roll to uncover a Clue that incorporates a Social Skill produces a Clue with the Tainted Tag.<br /> <br /> For supernatural abilities the Storyteller must use their own judgement. Teleinfomatics' Deep Background will be thrown off my inconsistencies between the Splinter's background and their behaviour during the murder and Polygraph will only reveal that the Splinter genuinely believes &quot;it wasn't me&quot;, but Postcognition could catch the Splinter changing between personalities.<br /> <br /> <b>Split </b>(Scourge)<br /> <br /> Talent: Physical Psyche: As the living embodiment of a repressed personality trait a Split's dark side is not bound by the limits of the flesh. A Split who's good side repressed his anger may bestow his dark side with the ability to enter a berserker rage, while one who developed then repressed pyrophillia after a childhood trauma may control fire itself. Most Splits have simple dread powers that enhance their physical capabilities, the rest have psychic phenomina. If a Split wants more occult or magical abilities they have to crack open a tome like anyone else.<br /> <br /> <b>Stranger</b><br /> <br /> (Note, I think the Stranger write up is too focused on becoming supernatural. It should have more support for Buffalo Bill style attempts to become a different kind of human)<br /> <br /> <b>Talent \u2013 Occult Modus Operandi</b>: The Stranger's murders are part of a deeper occult pattern, it's not enough to heterochromes and discet their eyes for the occult secrets within. They must kill them under the light of a full moon while a north wind blows. And occult rituals, they have a momentum all of their own. Once per scene, when the Stranger intends to commit murder, they may roll Intelligence + Occult vs Resolve + Potency. Successes automatically inflicts a Condition on the victim (usually Spooked), and until the Condition is Resolved the Stranger gets 8-again in all rolls directly targeting their victim.<br /> <br /> <b>Frailty \u2013 No Heart But Another\u2019s</b>: At his very core, the Stranger seeks to become something else because he hates what he his. He is not comfortable in his own skin, and everyone can tell. When the Stranger makes an Expression, Persuasion, or Socialize roll, he makes it at a -3 penalty at all times. If he is pursuing a quarry, he can spend Willpower to offset the penalty and even risk Willpower to ensure great success, but in all other cases, the Stranger\u2019s true emptiness shines through.<br /> <br /> <b>Transcendent </b><br /> <br /> <b>Talent \u2013 Transcendent Terror</b>: The Transcendent was right, for all that they appear mortal their rituals, alchemy and murder worked. Transcendants gain a free dot of Dread Powers every time they kill. These Dread Powers must relate to the Transcendent's desired form, one who wishes to be a vampire will never weild power over fire or sunlight.<br /> <br /> <b>Frailty \u2013 Only Human</b>: The Transcendent may believe he has grown beyond the bonds of humanity, but in many ways, he is still fettered to the corpse of his old self. His weakness lies in being reminded that he is still mortal, and his \u201ctrue self\u201d is mere decoration added to human clay. Each Transcendent has a trigger, it might be hearing their old mortal name, or their mother's perfume, something that reminds them of everything they hated about themselves and want to escape. If the Trasncendent is exposed to this trigger they loose all their Dread Powers for the scene and immediately suffer a Breaking Point.<br /> <br /> <b>The Predator (Ripper)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Talent- I Have Your Scent</b><br /> A Predator fixates on his target. He stalks them, learns their habits, and savours every moment of the hunt. Once per scene, and only after making his target aware that they are being pursued, the Predator may roll Presence + Intimidation vs the targets Composure. If the Predator wins he earns a Stalking Point, up to a maximum of Intimidation. Stalking Points can only be spent in the scene where the Predator attempts to kill his pray, and only once per turn. Each point can:<ul><li>Remove the target's Defence for a turn.</li> <li>Double the successes on an attack roll, but only for the purposes of seeing if the attack inflicts a Tilt.</li> <li>Provide Wits automatic successes on a Stealth roll.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>The Beast (Scourge)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Talent- Top of the Food Chain</b><br /> <br /> Those who encounter a Beast feel the full effect of their animalistic nature. The Beast may use Stalking Points in the following additional ways. All of these require a successful Presence + Intimidation vs Composure + Potency roll.<ul><li>Reduce all the target's Mental Skills by Intimidation to a minimum of zero for a scene.</li> <li>Reduce the target's Firearms Skill by Intimidation to a minimum of zero for a scene.</li> <li>Trigger the fight response; the target will attempt to engage the Predator in melee combat until they are Beaten Down or dead.</li> <li>Trigger the flight response; the target will attempt to flee the Predator on foot.</li> <li>Assert dominance over another predator, either a mundane animal, a Predator, or another Beast; the target will lie down and show throat, or it's species equivalent.</li> </ul><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T14:16:12-07:00","id":1134606,"title":"","content":"The copy of the Splinters and Splits I had actually came with an alternate set of Talents and Frailties. I have no idea whose alterations these were.<br /> <br /> <b>Splinters<br /> <i>Alternate Splinter Talent</i></b><b> \u2013 <i>A Strange Case: </i></b><i>The Splinter is an entirely separate personality, which means the Jekyll is very good at convincing people they aren't a murderer, because in a completely literal sense they are not. They add their Wits as automatic successes to all Persuasion rolls to convince others of their innocence. By hiding behind it's other half a Splinter remains ahead of their pursuit.</i><br /> <i>There are some logical limits to this advantage. If the Jekyll personality actually has committed a crime they cannot benefit from A Strange Case against that particular crime, nor do they get any benefits if directly questioned about split personalities or mental illness. The other logical limit is that the Jekyll has to cover for their darker side, but remember that Splinters are created because part of the Jekyll wants to murder. They create their other personality to commit the crimes they are unable too, most cover for their Hyde.</i><br /> <i>Splinters share their Attributes and Physical Merits between both selves. Skills, other Merits, Virtues, Vices, Codes and Integrity may differ. Both have a separate Willpower pool. The Hyde reverses the mechanics for Virtue and Vice.</i><br /> <b><i>Alternate Splinter Frailty</i></b><b> \u2013 <i>A Warning Light Glimmering In Red: </i></b><i>The murderer within can only come out at certain times. Each Splinter has a trigger and when it's pressed the dark side takes over for one scene at which point it must do everything in its power to commit murder before their time is up. Splinters don't have the luxury of planning; they kill on the whims of their psychosis. After the deed is done the Hyde has the remainder of the scene to cover up the deed from the law or their other half, but some Splinters relinquish control early and let their better half take care of the cover up.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Splits<br /> <i>Alternate Split Talent</i></b><b> \u2013 <i>Who is this Creature that I See: </i></b><i>Splits are two different people, literally. When either personality takes over they physically transform. The Jekyll and Hyde can look almost identical or as different as a mother and son, but they're always recognizable as different people and always have a strong family resemblance.</i><br /> <i>What this means in practical terms is that Splits are highly resistant to forensic profiling. Though genetic analysis reveals a family connection it also clearly points away from the innocent personality, fingerprints say likewise. What's more the Jekyll is the original, so the Hyde is created fresh with no presence on any database. This of course can look odd but in the World of Darkness most law enforcement will accept flimsy explanations in favor of a supernatural transformation.</i><br /> <i>This transformation effect extends beyond the body by a few meters. If there's a few hairs on the jacket the Split is wearing when he transforms that get left behind at the scene of the crime, those will have transformed too.</i><br /> <i>If a Split develops further Talents, they only apply while their darker side is in control.</i><br /> <b><i>Alternate Split Frailty</i></b><b> \u2013 <i>Free: </i></b><i>A Splinter was created as an excuse to commit the crimes the Jekyll couldn't. A Split is free from its creator, its own murderous person. The two halves hate each other. Each side has three triggers (one of which comes from A Warning Light Glimmering In Red). When one of the dormant personalities\u2019 triggers is pressed, roll Resolve vs. Resolve. If the dormant personality wins control is reversed.</i><br /> <i>While Splits start with identical Resolve one side may raise Resolve above its counterpart. This imbalance is psychological unhealthy for the weaker party and a Persistent Condition should be inflicted as a result. If the Hyde gains a Talent that boosts his Resolve a more severe Persistent Condition should be chosen, one likely to cause trouble for both personalities.</i><br /> <br /> I know that I added them in but I don't remember where they came from or who they were by. Will still add these as alternate Talents and Frailties for Strangers/Transcendent and updated Talents for Predators/Beasts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1417,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","user":"Reaper Verse","date":". 08-27-2017, 05:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T18:30:15-07:00","id":1134698,"title":"","content":"Hey guys, just got a heads-up from a friend, they said that maybe the Talents and Frailties for Splinter and Split are a little <i>too</i> close to the real DID. Maybe we can rework it slightly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T18:34:53-07:00","id":1134699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1127469-fan-group-pdf?p=1134698#post1134698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey guys, just got a heads-up from a friend, they said that maybe the Talents and Frailties for Splinter and Split are a little <i>too</i> close to the real DID. Maybe we can rework it slightly?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ...for which Talent and Frailty because we have 3 separate renditions now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T18:46:52-07:00","id":1134700,"title":"","content":"PM me the three versions and I'll read them over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T19:49:24-07:00","id":1134715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1127469-fan-group-pdf?p=1134698#post1134698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey guys, just got a heads-up from a friend, they said that maybe the Talents and Frailties for Splinter and Split are a little <i>too</i> close to the real DID. Maybe we can rework it slightly?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, I wanted to say something too, but I was too chicken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T20:19:28-07:00","id":1134727,"title":"","content":"Sent over. Predator/Beast has been revised and Stranger/Transcendent have their Alternates. Also wrote up a different Scourge Undertaking for Minders. Here are the Collectors.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Collector (Scourge)</b><br /> <i>\u2018You are just so\u2026beautiful.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> While a Minder entraps their victims and subjects them to severe mental and physical torment, they do acknowledge that their victims must, in time, leave them to make it out in the world. Minders cling to their victims because they care or try to care or want to care; they love their ward and their wellbeing is ultimately their goal (and if their ward passes, they will move on to the next). For all that they do, Minders still view their victims as human beings that deserve to be treated as such.<br /> <br /> For a Collector, they view their victims as objects: dolls, works of art, treasures. A Collector seeks out their victims without the twisted selflessness of a Minder, only focused on their own wants and desires. They abduct their victims because they needed a blonde to act as a sister in their decaying family dinner or because they have the perfect body structure to pose as The Thinker. The void in their life aches to be filled and they are more than willing to search out for that missing piece.<br /> <br /> While Minders use control as a means to gain authority, Collectors use control in order to enforce their idea of perfection. Everything about their victims is altered in order to bring their view out into reality. One Collector bashes in the kneecaps of an older woman in order to make her the spitting image of their grandmother, forced into a wheelchair and all. Another abducts conjoined twins in order create a \u201cmuseum of the strange\u201d, immobilizing them within a twisted display case.<br /> <br /> Eventually, a Collector\u2019s collection will start to break apart. Victims run, bodies decay, or maybe the Collector just saw fit to break their collection itself because there was <i>just one thing</i> that was off about it. However it happens, the Collector will be spurred to search for that next piece. And this time, they will make sure that their collection is <i>perfect</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>Background: </b>The main driving forces for a Collector are their obsessive thoughts and their want for completion. Whether they are haunted by memories of a broken house and smiling dolls or their desire to express their morbid taste in aesthetics, Collectors spend their days observing those around them like a mantis ready to snatch up its prey.<br /> <br /> Collectors often operate in periods; a successful abduction and efficient means of preserving their victims means that they may go from months to years without actively hunting. When they do go off on their hunt, they have a type that they are on a look out for. Thick arms with a shoulder tattoo, sunny red hair and skin kissed with freckles, a Collector\u2019s select target seldom differs from previous targets.<br /> <br /> Minders that prefer to immobilize their victims have a tendency to become Collectors; the ease of maintaining a still victim allows these Minders a greater degree of control that Collectors enjoy. The lack of response when interacting with the victims may even fuel the delusions that haunt Collectors. The key point in which a Minder begins to turn is when they realize that having only one is not as satisfying as having another, the indulgence is what causes their descent.<br /> <br /> Notably, Collectors often anthropomorphize their victims even after their death, playing out skits or having intense arguments. They reenact memories of a close, loving family or act out fantasies of protecting their loved ones. They dance with nobles and parade around sculptures, each victim playing the part of a background character to the Collector\u2019s grand delusion. To those uninitiated to the works of the Collector, these scenes may even seem as real to them as they are to the Collector.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Inspirations: </i></b><i>Sander Cohen (Bioshock), Doctor X (The Cat Lady), Professor Henry Jarrod (House of Wax)</i><br /> <br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Manipulation or Composure<br /> <br /> <b>Undertaking Skills: Crafts, </b>Investigation, Medicine, Brawl, Weaponry, Empathy, Expression, Persuasion, Socialization, Subterfuge<br /> <br /> <b>Talent \u2013 Real to Me: </b>Collectors have immersed themselves deeply into their delusion, seeing a world that exists only in their minds. However, that world empowers them, feeding their fantasy and fueling their actions. When a Collector is within the same location (roughly an average building or a small open field) with at least one of their victims, they can bring part of their delusion into the real world. The Collector may position their victims as if their victims were alive and capable of movement. This only occurs if the bodies are unnoticed but may occur even if the Collector cannot physically manipulate the victim or is otherwise indisposed.<br /> Furthermore, if the Collector can visibly see at least one of his victims, they become emboldened, working with the strength and ability of many. The Collector\u2019s physical rolls are treated as if they had benefitted from teamwork (roll Manipulation + Composure once for the teamwork bonus).<br /> <br /> <b>Frailty \u2013 My Strange Obsession: </b>A Collector\u2019s mind is firmly rooted in the strength of their collection; there is nothing more important than maintaining their collection. Collectors are affected with the Fugue Persistent Condition with the trigger being a new addition to their collection. When the Collector sees a target that matches up with a motif from their collection, they trigger Fugue and automatically fail the Condition. They become locked in their daze until either the end of the scene, until they lose sight of their target, or they are attacked.<br /> This obsession extends to the safety of their collection; though their reaction is on the opposite side of the spectrum. When a Collector notices that their Collection has been tampered with, they fly into a frenzy, gaining the Fixated Condition with the command being \u201cInflict hell on the person that damaged my collection\u201d. If the tampering occurs outside of the Collector\u2019s notice or is due to a natural or otherwise nonhuman occurrence, the Collector directs their fury towards the next living person they meet.<br /> <br /> <i><b>VASCU Case Study: Prince Charming</b></i><br /> <i>Transcribed from a letter found on the body of one Melissa Poe, 23. Poe was dressed in a custom-fit evening gown and tiara when police found her body at a downtown park. Contents of the letter appear to be the same as the Charming case 7 years ago. Sent to evidence for processing.<br /> <br /> &quot;My Dearest Angel,<br /> <br /> When you failed to wake on that soft Tuesday morning I had feared that the spectre of death had come to take you away from me. I pressed my ear against your chest to once again hear your beating heart but it was nothing more than the silence that keeps me up at night. My darling Angel, I watched each sunbeam fall onto your cold cheek as your body hung limp in my arms. Why, why did the spectre choose you to take?<br /> <br /> &quot;But with a kiss, you stirred in my arms and I felt the weight of your endless joy in your body, my sweet! Our Love! Our Love is what brought you back to the waking world! I knew you were weak from your sleep but I drew your bath as you sang those beautiful words that you spoke to me those many years. Though, such words could only come second to your radiance.<br /> <br /> &quot;My Angel, I write to you to remind you of the memories we have made. To remind you of the stars that graced us with their light and allowed me to bask in your alabaster glow. To remind you of the days we would stroll through the garden and tease the thought of one day eloping. To remind you of the time we shared dancing through the halls of my soon-to-be maison. To remind you of all that when you run from me once again. But, as always, I shall remain here, faithful, until the day you run back into my arms.<br /> <br /> &quot;Til that day comes, I wish you safety.<br /> <br /> &quot;Farewell,<br /> <br /> &quot;Your Prince Charming&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T00:16:00-07:00","id":1134774,"title":"","content":"Splinters/Splits are based on Dr Jekyll, I'm not sure there is any way to write them that doesn't resemble disassociative identity disorder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T08:19:51-07:00","id":1134840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1127469-fan-group-pdf?p=1134571#post1134571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which reminds me, should look into LostLight's versions of Endowments for Compacts as well. We also have some alternate Endowments in general (one of the big ones being Gospels for MM). Gonna add that one soon. Chapter 4 is building up to be respectably chunky.</div> </div> </div> </div>Things like alternative Endowments, Conspiracy Endowment level for Compacts or things like the Civil War project could be added as an extra chapter meant for Shards, which may make things a bit more organized. Chapter 4 may also include Kings idea for &quot;Big Guns Endowments&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T12:25:23-07:00","id":1134898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1127469-fan-group-pdf?p=1134774#post1134774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Splinters/Splits are based on Dr Jekyll, I'm not sure there is any way to write them that doesn't resemble disassociative identity disorder.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The only way I can think of it not resembling DID is to rework it as a person who lives secret lives and trades in their identities when they no longer need to use it, like Henry Morrison/Jerry Blake/etc. from The Stepfather or some Black Widow-type characters. Or it could be that the person is projecting a persona that they view as a different person. It makes the Undertaking less based on a medical condition and more based on their actions and compulsions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T12:27:42-07:00","id":1134899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1127469-fan-group-pdf?p=1134898#post1134898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The only way I can think of it not resembling DID is to rework it as a person who lives secret lives and trades in their identities when they no longer need to use it, like Henry Morrison/Jerry Blake/etc. from The Stepfather or some Black Widow-type characters. Or it could be that the person is projecting a persona that they view as a different person. It makes the Undertaking less based on a medical condition and more based on their actions and compulsions.</div> </div> </div> </div>First one is so much better. Let's flesh that out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T13:04:22-07:00","id":1134908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1127469-fan-group-pdf?p=1134898#post1134898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only way I can think of it not resembling DID is to rework it as a person who lives secret lives and trades in their identities when they no longer need to use it, like Henry Morrison/Jerry Blake/etc. from The Stepfather or some Black Widow-type characters. Or it could be that the person is projecting a persona that they view as a different person. It makes the Undertaking less based on a medical condition and more based on their actions and compulsions.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you do that it wouldn't be Splinter/Split at all. It's a completely different concept. If you want to ditch the Undertaking entirely I won't stop you, but I do think that the only way to avoid a Splinter/Splits resembling DID is to drop them entirely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T13:21:51-07:00","id":1134917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1127469-fan-group-pdf?p=1134908#post1134908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you do that it wouldn't be Splinter/Split at all. It's a completely different concept. If you want to ditch the Undertaking entirely I won't stop you, but I do think that the only way to avoid a Splinter/Splits resembling DID is to drop them entirely.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They are kinda cool, but how mad would you be if we took the suggestion about just dropping them to avoid the &quot;real-world neuro-atypical people are inherently monsters&quot; implications? I know Jekyll/Hyde-types are classics, but so are a lot of other tropes Onyx Path has avoided.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T14:06:27-07:00","id":1134942,"title":"","content":"I don't think there is any &quot;real-world neuro-atypical people are inherently monsters&quot; implications though. Nothing about Splinters says that murdering is an inherent result of DID rather than the Undertaking being a special unique case. The only implication that would bother me is the idea we need to be treated with kid gloves, if it's ok to base an Undertaking on neurotypical traits it's ok to base an Undertaking on neuro-atypical traits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T14:25:03-07:00","id":1134948,"title":"","content":"Well, Flyboy stated that it was more a concern over the Talents and Frailties rather than the basis of the Splinters/Splits. It may be something in the execution of the Talents that hits too close to home or implies something about DID. They haven't messaged me back about it yet so I'm hoping at least one of the iterations of their Talents/Frailties pass.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T12:42:04-07:00","id":1135249,"title":"","content":"so I've finished going through <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1wc9SK8owjHEo5uZDwu0lvJaEtedV6axZEXpZ1hp8xnY/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Raziel's </a>writeup and fixing any spelling and grammar mistakes I've found. I imagine some have escaped my attention, so I'll appreciate if someone else could give it a look. Also, currently Raziel has 8 example Endowments in their writeup. Is that enough? And if not, how many do you think are needed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T18:51:46-07:00","id":1135313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1127469-fan-group-pdf?p=1135249#post1135249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so I've finished going through <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1wc9SK8owjHEo5uZDwu0lvJaEtedV6axZEXpZ1hp8xnY/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Raziel's </a>writeup and fixing any spelling and grammar mistakes I've found. I imagine some have escaped my attention, so I'll appreciate if someone else could give it a look. Also, currently Raziel has 8 example Endowments in their writeup. Is that enough? And if not, how many do you think are needed?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Taking the nearest canon Conspiracy with a similar Endowment (VALKYRIE and their Advanced Armory), it's relatively fine. Advanced Armory had 10 to start but varied the cost, with both Ethereal Rounds and the Mjolnir Cannon being the only 5 Dot powers and those were still available at a lower level. If you can pump out two more, that'd make the Endowment more sizeable and well-rounded. Maybe at 3 and 4 Dots?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T20:22:23-07:00","id":1135335,"title":"","content":"My edit of Raziel Ltd writeup is done finally if you want to look it over and approve the changes, LostLight","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T01:30:48-07:00","id":1135369,"title":"","content":"Look what I found sitting around my documents folder<br /> <br /> These were an unusual one, in that I wrote them as antagonists for Vampires rather than protagonists.<br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Sunrise Securities</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Doorkeepers</span><br /> <br /> Slavery was one of the great evils of the 17th century. An entire people were ripped from their homes, their cultures, and taken into lives of hard labour and cruelty. Hundreds of years were not enough to erase the scars, but within every act of destruction lies the potential for new creation. Generations born upon foreign shores without the culture of their ancestors filled the void with acts of creation. Jazz, soul, hip hop; art and music flowed from the African Diaspora and shaped the world.<br /> <br /> But the monsters who lived and unlived in slavery\u2019s wake never left when the laws changed. If Vampires cannot buy people to profit and drink from then the club scene, with it\u2019s late nights and inebriated patrons, makes a modern replacement. But it is no longer 1860, tonight African America stands strong in their castles, they fill the halls with music and they bar the door against the monsters outside.<br /> <br /> Sunrise Securities was formed by accident at the Corn and Rooster, a harlem jazz club owned and operated by Reginald \u201cdoctor\u201d Cobra: entrepreneur, b\u00f2k\u00f4non, and a fairly decant hand on the keyboard. At it\u2019s height the Corn and Rooster was the place to be for Harlem locals, and white folk slumming it for the good music. By day the club rehearsed, by night the club danced, and upon holy days the club partied with the Loa. For a time all was good.<br /> <br /> Dancers and music lovers weren\u2019t the only people drawn to the Corn and Rooster. With time and experience Reginald began to grow suspicious, he saw regulars leaving with different people every visit, people who always woke up weak the next day. He turned to spells and divinations, and when he knew what manner of leach was succking at the lifeblood of his establishment, he acted. Reginald gathered his employees and performed a grand ritual and petitioned Papa Legba, the Loa who guards all gates, to make his club a sacred space. Safe from the predators which stalked the night outside.<br /> <br /> With the Loa\u2019s blessing business boomed, nobody said a word but everyone knew that the Corn and Rooster was the safest club in town. Reginald\u2019s rivals began to grumble, and in their grumblings Reginald saw a business opportunity. Sunrise Securities was formed.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Enemy</span><br /> <br /> Let other Hunters venture into dark places and fight the monsters within. Sunrise Securities has their own mission: This place is sacred, this music is sacred, and none shall disturb it. Whatever happens outside these four walls is somebody else\u2019s business, at least for as long as they\u2019re on the clock.<br /> <br /> Vampires are Sunrise Securities\u2019 most common foe. The image of the glamourous, sexy, Vampire stalking the dance floor is well known for a reason, Vampires really do like to prey upon nightclubs and as far as Sunrise Securities are concerned if they see a Vampire they show him the door. Vampires\u2019 are also the most vulnerable to the Compact\u2019s Endowment (after all, Reginald petitioned Papa Legba for a tool against Vampires, and he got what he asked for). <br /> <br /> After Vampires come Changelings, the second most likely supernatural being to turn up at a nightclub. A Changeling\u2019s emotional harvesting is far less harmful than a vampire\u2019s drinking so Sunrise Securities are more tolerant. Their bouncers can recite the standard pledge of good behaviour from memory in their sleep. Besides, Changelings can make some damn fine music. Some Freeholds even hire Sunrise Securities to provide bouncers for their own clubs, and the firm sees nothing wrong with taking the contract. Mostly though, Changelings stay beneath Sunrise\u2019s radar.<br /> <br /> There are other monsters who stalk the night looking for human pray. Beasts talk a good game about having a higher purpose, but at the end of the day if they get hungry an intoxicated clubber is easy prey. Sunrise Securities on the whole are in favour of otherworldly beings teaching humans lessons that are needed if not always kind. They call those beings the Loa, and they don\u2019t like the idea of amateurs bungling the job, especially if it hurts or traumatises one of their protectees. However Beasts are powerful, and few Doorkeepers will willingly take one on alone.<br /> <br /> Picture: A middle aged and very muscular african american in a bad suit, the kind of man you might describe as a brick. He's wearing many gold chains, one of which has Papa Legba's Veve.<br /> <br /> <b>You! Beat it!</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Stereotypes</span><br /> <br /> The Union: It\u2019s disappointing how often \u201cprotecting our neighbours\u201d stops where the ghetto begins. But they know how to fight so we\u2019ll ask for their help. Duty before pride brother.<br /> <br /> Ascending Ones: Monsters around here have an odd habit of disappearing. I don\u2019t know who\u2019s doing it, but there\u2019s a drink waiting for him behind the bar.<br /> <br /> Night Watch: You don\u2019t push, you don\u2019t bring your piece past this door, and we don\u2019t have a problem.<br /> <br /> The Staff of Janus: I ain\u2019t going to faerieland, not for money or magic. I\u2019ve got my door and my music right here.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Status</span><br /> <br /> Status in Sunrise Securities is a formal affair handled by human resources. In a nutshell the longer you\u2019ve worked for Sunrise, and the longer you\u2019ve gone without screwing up, the higher your status.<br /> <br /> O: You\u2019ve gone through Sunrise Securities corporate training program. Take a dot of Trained Observer and a dot of Doorkeeping.<br /> OOO: You\u2019re an old hand, and have seen a bit in your time. Take two dots in the Street Fighting Merit as a momento of your experiences.<br /> OOOOO: You\u2019re as much of a fixture of the club scene as the clubs themselves. Everyone around knows your name, take the Barfly Merit and a dot of Contacts in the club scene.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Endowment: Doorkeeping (O - OOOOO)</span><br /> <br /> Bouncers employed by Sunrise Security are trained in the sacred, and humbly named, art of Doorkeeping. A sacred contract in which the bouncer assumes responsibility for the safety of all within their building. Sunrise's employees may be professional or they may take bribes. Some are polite and helpful, others like to throw their weight around. But nothing: Not money, not pride, not the club management, will stop a Doorkeeper from doing whatever it takes to ensure everyone visiting their establishment is protected until they\u2019re safely on their way home.<br /> <br /> The more dedicated they are to this duty the greater the potency of this Endowment, but even a single dot requires a firm commitment.<br /> <br /> Doorkeeping grants the following benefits while on duty:<ul><li>Doorkeeper may Risk Willpower an additional Doorkeeping times a scene, providing they use their extra risks on rolls benefiting from Doorkeeping.</li> <li>Add Doorkeeping to all rolls to notice trouble. This could be a Perception roll, a Wits + Empathy roll to notice someone\u2019s looking for trouble, a Wits + Occult roll to recognise a vampire, or even a Wits + Medicine roll to notice someone\u2019s reacting badly to drugs.</li> <li>Against Obscurificate and other similar vampiric powers a Doorkeeper automatically rolls Wits + Doorkeeping as a Clash of Wills.</li> <li>Each Dot of Doorkeeping provides an automatic Successes on Contested rolls to resist being persuaded, intimidated, or mind controlled into overlooking trouble in a Doorkeeper\u2019s premise. If the roll is Resisted the other character subtracts Doorkeeping Successes from their roll instead. Against Dominate, Majesty, or other similar vampiric abilities the effect grows to two Successes.</li> <li>If a Doorkeeper tells a vampire they can't enter or to get out of their premise they may roll Presence + Intimidation + Doorkeeping vs Composure + Potency. If the Doorkeeper wins the vampire becomes psychologically unable to enter, and if they\u2019re inside they must leave immediately. The effect lasts until sunrise, or until the Doorkeeper's death.</li> </ul><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T07:48:03-07:00","id":1135444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1127469-fan-group-pdf?p=1135313#post1135313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Taking the nearest canon Conspiracy with a similar Endowment (VALKYRIE and their Advanced Armory), it's relatively fine. Advanced Armory had 10 to start but varied the cost, with both Ethereal Rounds and the Mjolnir Cannon being the only 5 Dot powers and those were still available at a lower level. If you can pump out two more, that'd make the Endowment more sizeable and well-rounded. Maybe at 3 and 4 Dots?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll try- but each Theo Tech does require some work and research- I need to go to the bible, search for a verse which sounds really interesting and then base a new Endowment around it. I'll see what I can do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T11:13:14-07:00","id":1135513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1127469-fan-group-pdf?p=1135369#post1135369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look what I found sitting around my documents folder<br /> <br /> These were an unusual one, in that I wrote them as antagonists for Vampires rather than protagonists.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not exactly 100% sure, but the Brotherhood of the Locust is in and I think they're technically more for WtF than HtV. I presume that Sunset is leaning more towards Compact?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T11:42:09-07:00","id":1135521,"title":"","content":"They're a Compact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T13:11:15-07:00","id":1135565,"title":"","content":"Thanks TKR. I'll put that down in the books.<br /> <br /> -----<br /> <br /> Should probably do an update about our numbers. Insofar:<br /> <br /> <b>12 Compacts</b> out of our current <b>29 total Compacts</b> are considered complete.<br /> <br /> <b>17 Conspiracies</b> out of our staggering <b>59 total Conspiracies</b> are considered complete.<br /> <br /> <b>6 Cults, Cabals, etc.</b> out of our <b>17 total Cults, Cabals, etc</b>. are considered complete.<br /> <br /> That makes <b>35 complete Organizations</b> out of <b>105 total Organizations</b> being fully complete.<br /> <br /> The average write-up consists of 1 splash page and 2 written pages, with 1-2 extra pages given to account for formatting. This means that, bare minimum, Chapters 1-3 will account for <b>175 pages;</b> 60 pages for Compacts, 85 pages for Conspiracies, and 30 pages for Cults, Cabals, etc. This does not include outliers such as Schutzgruppe, which increases their specific page number by 3+ pages. This also does not include Endowments, which I am unsure if we want to include in the organizations themselves or move them into the Endowment section of Chapter 4. This would be roughly...let's say 2-4 pages each, probably 50 pages total with variation. That brings up the estimated minimum page total to <b>225 pages plus change</b>.<br /> <br /> For comparison, <b>Dream Catchers</b> is about 247 pages while <b>Skin and Bones </b>is 116 pages not including the chopped Compacts and Conspiracies. The official Hunter: the Vigil book is a little less than 400 pages. The splat books for Vampires, Werewolves, and Mages are all shy of 250.<br /> <br /> By these numbers, we are going to create a rather substantial fanbook. There are a few organizations that are only &quot;incomplete&quot; because they lack a Stereotype section; it would be marvelous if we can get this organizations up and running. After that, it would be good for us to actually cut some of the organizations that are &quot;weaker&quot; out before working on completing any other Organization. Personally, I feel that my own organization, the Broker's Guild, is rather weakly-written and would like to either drop them or rewrite them entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T13:15:18-07:00","id":1135566,"title":"","content":"We're definitely imbalanced towards conspiracies.<br /> <br /> But dare I say it, if we can condense some of the wordier write-ups, I think we might come to a reasonable page number","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 08-30-2017, 05:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T14:18:17-07:00","id":1135594,"title":"","content":"Also:<br /> <br /> 1) Do the complete ones still need editing?<br /> <br /> 2) Is this counting the fan-Undertakings?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T15:13:14-07:00","id":1135619,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:24px\"><u><b>Organizations that are missing Only One Section (Excluding Factions): </b></u></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>COMPACTS:</b></span><br /> <b>*Bookhounds of London </b><i><b>(Status)</b></i><br /> <br /> <b>*The Fire Starters </b><i><b>(Status)</b></i><br /> <br /> Maagal HaBaal VehaAshera <i>(Hunters)</i><br /> <br /> Maw of the River <i>(Hunters)</i><br /> <br /> <b>*The Parabalani </b><i><b>(Hunters)</b></i><br /> <br /> <b><s>*Ride to Damascus</s></b><s><i><b> (Hunters)</b></i></s><br /> <br /> Shepherds of Annwn <i>(Hunters)</i><br /> <br /> <b>*Sunrise Securities </b><i><b>(Hunters)</b></i><br /> <br /> <b>*The Underworld Syndicate </b><i><b>(Hunters)</b></i><br /> <br /> Venerators of the Old Gods <i>(Status)</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>CONSPIRACIES:</b></span><br /> Aki Ten <i>(Hunters)</i><br /> <br /> al-Rih al-Asuad <i>(Hunters)</i><br /> <br /> <i>[[[Avici Sutra (Hunters)]]]</i><br /> <br /> Burya Storozh <i>(Hunters)</i><br /> <br /> <b>*The Carpenters </b><i><b>(The Enemy)</b></i><br /> <br /> Followers of Set <i>(Hunters)</i><br /> <br /> Heirs of the Crown <i>(Hunters)</i><br /> <br /> Her Majesty's Royal Order of Supernatural Defenders <i>(The Enemy)</i><br /> <br /> <b>*KSI 21 </b><i><b>(Hunters)</b></i><br /> <br /> Navio de Tolos <i>(Hunters)</i><br /> <br /> The Nibiru <i>(Hunters)</i><br /> <br /> <b><s>*R.A.M. </s></b><s><i><b>(Hunters)</b></i></s><br /> <br /> Tiensheng <i>(Hunters)</i><br /> <br /> The Usij <i>(Hunters)</i><br /> <br /> Yam VeHar Factories <i>(Hunters)</i><br /> <br /> The Zmei Initiative <i>(Hunters)</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>CULTS, CABALS, ETC.</b></span><br /> <b>*The Knights Errant </b><i><b>(Stereotypes)</b></i><br /> <br /> <b>*Hearth of Hestia </b><i><b>(Hunters)</b></i><br /> <br /> <i>[[[The Apollonian Priesthood (Hunters)]]]</i><br /> <br /> <b>*Los Innocentes <i>(The Enemy)</i></b> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><u><b>Organizations that are missing Only Two Sections (Excluding Factions): </b></u></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>COMPACTS:</b></span><br /> <b><s>*LLannerch Athrawon (Hunters, Stereotypes)</s></b><br /> <br /> The Silent Imperative (The Enemy, Hunters)<br /> <br /> The Silv