"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T14:34:18-07:00","id":1136375,"title":"","content":"I have been watching this thread with no small amount of awe and envy!<br /> <br /> I just wanted a little feedback for my Shih write up - wanted to see if there was any language that can be tweaked or blank spots to fill in. I am especially interested in the stereotypes. I have tried a few times to come up with something, but so far I can quite get the voice needed for that section - any suggestions would be welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T14:49:48-07:00","id":1136381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1127469-fan-group-pdf?p=1136375#post1136375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have been watching this thread with no small amount of awe and envy!<br /> <br /> I just wanted a little feedback for my Shih write up - wanted to see if there was any language that can be tweaked or blank spots to fill in. I am especially interested in the stereotypes. I have tried a few times to come up with something, but so far I can quite get the voice needed for that section - any suggestions would be welcome.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The thing I noticed with the Shih is that the feel of the organization is very...antiquated? Mainly, the language makes the organization feel that they are still in the Dynastic Age. It does mention a bit about how the way of the Shih is incredibly difficult, unrewarding, and may lead to problematic behavior to cope, which is great. However, they could have a bit more modernistic flavor, especially when it comes to the bitterness.<br /> <br /> Also, I would be interested in hearing about a Shih disciple who gave up EVERYTHING to be a Shih disciple, stripping off all personality from their self in order to become a demon hunter (and ironically being known as a demon from those who only know about them by word-of-ear).<br /> <br /> As for Stereotypes, there are a few added in the document for the Shih in the Drive. I don't know whose Stereotypes those are though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T15:03:21-07:00","id":1136387,"title":"","content":"Speaking of Stereotypes, done! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T16:22:43-07:00","id":1136424,"title":"","content":"<b>Re: Stereotypes</b><br /> <br /> Thank You. This jars loose some of the creative block I was having. I can now see a figure sort of like &quot;Egg Shen&quot; from big trouble in little china. Wise, Powerful, but gruff and kind of disreputable.<br /> <br /> <b>Re: Modernity </b><br /> <br /> I wrote this quite some time ago not long after when Hunter:the Vigil first came out and the feeling of the venue was still being defined, and I hewed pretty close to the OWoD version. I am going my text to see if I can revise some text to make them seem less like a relic of a bygone era (or make them painfully aware that they ARE relics of a bygone time). Suggestions are welcome!<br /> <br /> <b>Re: Other Questions</b><br /> <br /> Currently, the 5th dot of Status coveys 3 dots worth of Relics. Since I wrote this, I have learned not to reference mechanics in source books the player may not have. Can you good folks suggest a good balanced alternative benefit for that 5th dot?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T16:30:35-07:00","id":1136428,"title":"","content":"And that means Llannerch Athrawon is officially ready to be shipped. Sweet. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> So quick point of order: the page count estimate is actually pretty on point; the Compact pages that I have lain out plus the introduction pages reach just shy of 60 pages currently. We have the meat of the fanbook already figured out so how are we gonna do the trimmings? <br /> <br /> Each chapter should have a short little snippet of what is in it, just about a page's worth of information. Maybe a fiction before? That'd be 5 fictions in total, 4 chapter snippets (we already have the Introduction just about set).<br /> <br /> And we should think about clean-ups and cuts. Insofar, the majority of the cuts might be from the Conspiracies due to their overall number and length of each write-up (and including their Endowments at the end of their write-up. Chapter 4 is effectively entirely safe from cuts but it needs some filler text to deal with segues from Endowments to Slashers. There's also a few references to organizations that we don't have that I'll have to clean out (Harlequin's Roses, etc.) The book itself already has the layouts done and dealt with so anything that is officially finished can be thrown in, with dummy pages thrown in for those that don't have a splash page up yet (will get to that when I come home).<br /> <br /> If I had to quantify how far we are in terms of getting the book to full completion, I'd say we are at a respectable 45-55% done. 20% of what's missing is going to be images while the rest is mainly writing. And that isn't including the editing and polish phases. We're pretty solidly far but we basically need to get the prototype out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T04:39:29-07:00","id":1136546,"title":"","content":"added Hunters section for the R.A.M. I'll finish working on the Innocents sometime next week.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T15:03:48-07:00","id":1136724,"title":"","content":"Awesome! R.A.M. gets pushed up. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Because I'm effectively neutered for the rest of the week, I'm gonna do some quick statistics for the heck of it: looking at what splats organizations focus on, locale, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T13:26:41-07:00","id":1137429,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar503_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"503\" data-vbnamecard=\"503\">LostLight</a> want to team up for Hakollel's steryotypes and hunters section, on the basis that of the two of us you're actually Israeli.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T13:51:24-07:00","id":1137437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1127469-fan-group-pdf?p=1137429#post1137429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar503_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"503\" data-vbnamecard=\"503\">LostLight</a> want to team up for Hakollel's steryotypes and hunters section, on the basis that of the two of us you're actually Israeli.</div> </div> </div> </div>sure! I need to do something in my work other than watching the computer :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T15:03:13-07:00","id":1137462,"title":"","content":"Ah. I miss those slow days <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Anyway, the MM are obvious choices as the largest religious organisation. The Loyalists of Thule are a must, but I'm not sure what direction to take. Feel free to nominate one of your groups. For their voice, I imagine a slightly rambling and slightly teasing voice. &quot;I'm too old and wise to get worked up about things&quot;, a bit like Set Roth from Wolfenstein, except more cheerful because he's not living in a world ruled by Nazis. Maybe something like:<br /> <br /> Maidens Blood Sisterhood: That book was here yesterday. Ah, there it is. Lets see, apply olive oil... ah a warning, after sundown... yada yada. You should be fine bevmebl, smart girl like you should have nothing to worry about. Bring that back to me after class tomorrow and call your mother soon. You know she worries.<br /> <br /> (female Hunter --&gt; Deborah --&gt; bee --&gt; bumblebee sounds cuter --&gt; translate to yidish --&gt; romanise it --&gt; shorten it to make a nickname --&gt; bevembl. Mum wasn't around so if something went wrong I'm counting on you to correct me).<br /> <br /> I think somebody's sterotype on them should ask if their decision to use Shemot, rather than just study and guard them, was a sin. If I got my theology right it quite possibly is - and raising that question without answering it was intentional. But then again, it's also possible that the Abrahamic God is in fact the Principal which means real world theology might not apply in the first place. Another Steryotype saying that The Fire is just a natural force, why are they trying to have theological debates with it could also work.<br /> <br /> <br /> For the Hunters I want a mixture of different Jewish denominations along with one or two who origoninally hail from of weird barely Jewish sects that only exist in the WoD. Thus far the only Hunter I have is an ex-Mossad Rabbi and a Golem who travel the world and fight terrorism in zany buddy cop adventures.. <hr /><br /> I'll stop here and give you a chance to respond with your own ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 09-04-2017, 06:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-05T09:56:47-07:00","id":1137729,"title":"","content":"about your Yiddish translation- I can't help you with that. I don't know a word in that language- I took Arts and Philosophy classes in high school instead :P<br /> <br /> They should probably have a Stereotype about either the Malleus, the Long Night or the Order of St Anthony- and probably not a positive one, especially for the first. Jewish people, especially the religious ones, still remember things like the Inquisition or the blood libels, and while they probably won't be openly hostile toward them, they would see them as misguided at best or witches at worst. Even if they were to accept that God grants his blessing to them, they undoubtedly would remind you that whatever they can do is lesser when compared to &quot;true miracles&quot; preformed by jewish Tzadikim.<br /> <br /> If you were to include references to my homebrew groups, the Cage of Shadows is an heresy, and would be treated as such in their eyes. They also probably know the story about the Book of Raziel the Angel, and they probably have noticed that there is something fishy about Raziel Ltd. R.A.M has, without doubt, made a contact with them in Israel and they know that some self proclaimed Kabbalists has helped the development of Rukh Technology, but they have no idea how it works (as the powers behind the two Endowments are as distant as the skies are to earth- literally).<br /> <br /> Also, here is an example &quot;hunter&quot; writeup-<br /> <br /> You never understood those people who &quot;grow strong in their faith&quot;. In you world, there was no God- you believed only what you could see, hear and feel. Then, one night, just as you was on your way home after a party which got a little out of control- something jumped on you. Something twisted and horrifying and full of claws and teeth. You almost felt like your mind was breaking to pieces, and as you collapsed only two words has escaped your lips- Shema Israel. Surprisingly, it worked- the thing just stopped, turned around and left. You knew that no one among your family and friends would understand what happened, and so you turned to the only one that would- a rabbi. You were sure that he was going to call you crazy- but he didn't. Instead, he called for someone who &quot;knew the subject&quot; better than him. Since that night, you have grown stronger in your faith- and every time someone asked what happened, you only say the truth. That you only believe what you see- and that you saw God.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-05T12:58:59-07:00","id":1137802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1127469-fan-group-pdf?p=1137729#post1137729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They should probably have a Stereotype about either the Malleus, the Long Night or the Order of St Anthony- and probably not a positive one, especially for the first.</div> </div> </div> </div> Of those three I lean towards the Malleus, as they're more thematically &quot;pure&quot; than the Order with it's themes of communist persecution.<br /> <br /> But maybe it should be more of a sadness that Christianity doesn't live up to it's potential rather than hostility. It might fit better with the playful eccentric Dumbledoor-ish vibe I want to go for. And Judaism does have a strong streak of live and let live about other faiths. The Noahide Laws are really easy to uphold.<br /> <br /> <b>Malleus Maleficarum:</b> Yeshua, such a nice Jewish boy. I think he would be very sad to see what happened. His family should have found him a wife to settle down with, I think fatherhood would have been good for him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1127469-fan-group-pdf?p=1137729#post1137729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the Cage of Shadows is an heresy, and would be treated as such in their eyes.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Cage of Shadows:</b> Leave the land of your fathers, go to the sea of Erechtheus and bathe seven times. Do not return until you are clean, and go quickly for it pains me to send you away.<br /> <br /> (Erechtheus is a water Posideon created in a contest with Athena. Since the Strix have been linked to Athena before it felt like a good thing to use as a Bane; and the occult scholars in Hakollel are going to be busy researching banes for the Hunters they'd likely know about it)<br /> <br /> R.A.M. might be a good group to have an outsiders view on Hakollel. Something like &quot;The Fire is a thermodynamic force, it's occult physics. Why are you trying to debate theology with it?&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1127469-fan-group-pdf?p=1137729#post1137729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, here is an example &quot;hunter&quot; writeup-</div> </div> </div> </div>I like it. But why not use &quot;Elah Elahin&quot; instead of Shema Israel? As that Endowment forces monsters to flee.<br /> <br /> Here's another one.<br /> <br /> In your youth you led your congregation across the Middle East, through percecution from humans and monsters alike, until at last you arrived safely in the land of Israel. But you are an old man now, a younger Rabbi guides your old congregation and you have no more duties. Now you are free to walk old roads and travel the lands of your childhood. You follow whispers of forgotten lore and rumours of angels, for though you are an old man there is still time. Time to discover, to learn, to contemplate, and to become wise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 09-05-2017, 04:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-05T13:40:14-07:00","id":1137815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1127469-fan-group-pdf?p=1137802#post1137802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Malleus Maleficarum:</b> Yeshua, such a nice Jewish boy. I think he would be very sad to see what happened. His family should have found him a wife to settle down with, I think fatherhood would have been good for him.</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah, less of direct hostility and more of a condescending attitude works well for them. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> R.A.M. might be a good group to have an outsiders view on Hakollel. Something like &quot;The Fire is a thermodynamic force, it's occult physics. Why are you trying to debate theology with it?&quot; </div> </div> </div>well, I'm not sure how much R.A.M know about the Fire at the first place- but they are very suspicious of religious organizations which stray from the norm, as they are possible cults. Maybe something like &quot;you may look like a rabbi, but before I could trust you I need to make sure that your god is our God- for I have seen my share in my life, and they weren't pretty&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I like it. But why not use &quot;Elah Elahin&quot; instead of Shema Israel? As that Endowment forces monsters to flee. </div> </div> </div>well, Shema Israel is seen as the common &quot;last words&quot; a jewish says when they face death, so it felt appropriate. Maybe instead, the sentence would be something like &quot;and as you collapsed only two words has escaped your lips- Shema Israel. Or, at least that was what you meant to say, but other words came out&quot;. Something like that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-05T15:00:35-07:00","id":1137837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1127469-fan-group-pdf?p=1137815#post1137815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">yeah, less of direct hostility and more of a condescending attitude works well for them.</div> </div> </div> </div> Thanks. I'm glad you like it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1127469-fan-group-pdf?p=1137815#post1137815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">well, I'm not sure how much R.A.M know about the Fire at the first place</div> </div> </div> </div> Shame, it would have been good if someone could argue the non-religious interpretation of the fire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1127469-fan-group-pdf?p=1137815#post1137815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">well, Shema Israel is seen as the common &quot;last words&quot; a jewish says when they face death, so it felt appropriate. Maybe instead, the sentence would be something like &quot;and as you collapsed only two words has escaped your lips- Shema Israel. Or, at least that was what you meant to say, but other words came out&quot;. Something like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>IMO, keep it simple. One or the other.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-05T22:07:38-07:00","id":1137918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1127469-fan-group-pdf?p=1137837#post1137837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Shame, it would have been good if someone could argue the non-religious interpretation of the fire.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>mmmm perhaps the Nimrod Movement? Atheism is still something strong in the group, after all.<br /> <br /> for example:<br /> <br /> &quot;when the first people saw the sun, the lightning and the fire, they fell on their knees and believed them to be gods. You are doing the same, and you would have known it if you were to study something besides Torah. God is a lifeless mechanism, and you just worship the fire in its engines&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 09-06-2017, 01:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-06T00:33:28-07:00","id":1137936,"title":"","content":"I approve <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'd suggest capitalising the F in the final fire.<br /> <br /> Now what do we do for the Loyalists of Thule? <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 09-06-2017, 07:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-06T08:00:19-07:00","id":1138017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1127469-fan-group-pdf?p=1137936#post1137936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now what do we do for the Loyalists of Thule?</div> </div> </div> </div>well, a core principle of Judaism is that you could always redeem yourself (or to &quot;return to God&quot;), even after committing some terrible crimes and sins. While the Loyalists have all done something they regret and which harmed many others (like helping the Nazi Party at the start of their way), they have the right to find their way back to God- but it doesn't mean the Kollel needs to like them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-06T08:53:35-07:00","id":1138028,"title":"","content":"so, I have noticed that there is some mismatch between Reaper's list and Flyboy's list about the category of each of my organizations, so I've decided on posting a full list of my organizations according to the divide presented by the pitch, including some art suggestions. Hope it would help!<br /> <br /> <b><u>Compact</u></b><br /> Silent Imperative<br /> Silentium<br /> Tartaruchi (lost reach after the Purge)- the back of a man, scarred from whippings, his hands are dripping with blood<br /> Silver Syndicate- picture of Wall Street, with spirits clinging from the NYSE<br /> Lycos Agema<br /> Sabaoth- angel flying over a battlefield, divine light behind it while the ground is covered with many broken swords<br /> Maagal HaBaal VeHaAshera (formerly a Conspiracy)- something in the style of a circle of idols, crafted in an ancient middle eastren style<br /> Maw of the River- a person feeding a relic to a crocodile<br /> Theater of Tragedies- a scene from a brothel, with a masked woman with<br /> Nimrod Movement- two pages from the Book of Raziel, on one there is a picture of the Tower of Babylon and on the other an angel committing suicide<br /> MourningStar Developments<br /> <br /> <b><u>Conspiracy</u></b><br /> Raziel Ltd- a person using Genesis, surrounded by cords, wires and tubes which are all covered by occult symbols<br /> ZMEI Initiative<br /> Schrlach Spinnwebe- spider sitting in a center of a bloody web, each crossroad featuring an image of someone bitten by/drinking from a vampire<br /> Al Rih al Asuad<br /> Aki Ten- an Aki Ten hunter summoning one of their Shikigami in front of a Sakura Blossom<br /> Nibiru- nine hooded women standing before an eldritch horror, each holding a certain item<br /> Church of the Blood Moon- a young child sitting in a forest, the moon shines among the threes, playing the flute while surrounded by a pack of wolves<br /> Hrt Isfet<br /> Museum Secretorum<br /> A.S.T.R.A.L<br /> Nemontemi<br /> Custodes Ignis<br /> Penyihir Mayat<br /> Orchestra Fatalibus (may also be considered a Compact)<br /> Tiansheng<br /> Mori Kage- five shadowy figures hidden within a forest<br /> Chasseurs de Tetes (formerly a Cabal)- a bloody guillotine, beheaded heads are scattered all around it<br /> Ebony Fangs (barely)- the grim reaper, surrounded by scattered bones<br /> Tatau o te Po<br /> Eye of Heaven<br /> Avici Sutra<br /> R.A.M- the Tree of Life diagram, each Sphere showing a partial scene of the hunter's life<br /> Usij (may also be considered a Compact)<br /> Navio de Tolos- a captain standing on her ship, smiling against the wind while they go directly toward a sea serpent<br /> Knights of the Bloody Chalice<br /> Nightmare Network<br /> Burya Storozh<br /> Yam VeNahar Factories<br /> Benei Topheth- a figure going unharmed out of a burning building<br /> <br /> <b><u>Cult</u></b><br /> Apollonian Priesthood- a group of shirtless men, their hand in the air as they bath in the light of the sun<br /> Cage of Shadows- something which comes from from half BDSM room, half torture chamber, with an open cage hang in the middle<br /> Order of the Nameless- an eldritch horror contained in a magic circle, surrounded by broken mirrors<br /> Aga Nritya (could also be considered a Cabal)<br /> Garden of Hesperides- a beautiful gate covered with plants and flowers, which lead to a mysterious garden<br /> Shepherds of Annwn<br /> Pomegranate Deme<br /> Temple of Silence<br /> Heirs of the Crown<br /> Bone Collectors<br /> <br /> <b><u>Cabal</u></b><br /> Pythian Oracles- two hands on a crystal ball, before it are five tarot cards- the hermit, the devil, death, the moon and the tower, while a serpentine eye glimpse from the ball<br /> Los Inocentes<br /> E.V.E Institution<br /> Ashen Collective<br /> Cult of Moloch- the statue of a bull man, covered with flames<br /> <br /> <b><u>Cancer</u></b><br /> Tartarus Enterprise<br /> Followers of Set<br /> <br /> again, those art suggestions are just suggestions. I'll try to add the rest of those to each of my groups, but if you have a cool idea or that one those those just doesn't feel interesting enough for you, feel free to ignore them and go with the flow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 09-06-2017, 03:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-07T04:45:16-07:00","id":1138276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1127469-fan-group-pdf?p=1138017#post1138017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">well, a core principle of Judaism is that you could always redeem yourself (or to &quot;return to God&quot;), even after committing some terrible crimes and sins. While the Loyalists have all done something they regret and which harmed many others (like helping the Nazi Party at the start of their way), they have the right to find their way back to God- but it doesn't mean the Kollel needs to like them.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>The Loyalists of Thule:</b> Anyone can return to god, even you. Go seek your redemption, seek it far away from me.<br /> <br /> I think to finish off we need another positive stereotypy. Maybe the Hearth of Hestia: community spirit, traditional values, and I don't think Hakollel would care about people converting to the worship of Hestia just so long as it wasn't Jews converting. It's not like the Hearth break any Noahide laws.<br /> <br /> <b>Hearth of Hestia:</b> What a wonderful meal. You shouldn't go to the trouble to cook a kosher roast when your vegetables are such a delight... and I won't tell your pastor what you have done with your oven. It will be our little secret baleboste.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 09-07-2017, 05:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-08T11:06:45-07:00","id":1138641,"title":"","content":"Hakollel are now done. except for art. There's been a lot of tweaks to them over the years - so while I recommend getting the final version of all my groups from the forums this goes double for Hakollel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T09:17:55-07:00","id":1138907,"title":"","content":"*Dusts off sand* Sorry, had to focus on my training. What's the latest updates?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T10:03:09-07:00","id":1138920,"title":"","content":"Insofar, Llannerch Athrawon, R.A.M., and Hakollel Hamerkava are fully-written with Llannerch having a full art and the other two to be done when I get home from Arizona.<br /> <br /> I PM'ed you about the Splinter/Split issue. If the issue about their portrayal is solely in their Talent/Frailty, we can definitely fix that. If the issue lies within the write-up itself, the easiest way to deal with them is to axe them completely. Your call as you were the first to bring it up.<br /> <br /> Working on a statistics chart for the completed organizations. Surprisingly, a good chunk of the Compacts were established in the US as well as a few which are deliberately vague. Less of a pertinent part of the book and more of a little infographic.<br /> <br /> We definitely need some write-ups to open up each Chapter and some sections. Just about a half a page to a page per Chapter or so. It's something that we don't need immediately but it's something to think about.<br /> <br /> We might also need to do a chop. Dunno what criteria we should use to start making cuts though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T10:34:49-07:00","id":1138932,"title":"","content":"I'll handle the intro writeups. The problem was the Talents/Frailties, my friend stated that the writeups were fine.<br /> <br /> I think we need to look at which organizations were already covered in other fan pieces. Example, the Carpenters vs the Lord Stewards. Are they the same group, and does that mean we don't need the Carpenters. Kings, your thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T10:45:49-07:00","id":1138934,"title":"","content":"So what proposals do people have for the Talent/Frailtey? I don't see how you could do Jekyll/Hyde justice without it looking like dissociative identity disorder to some extent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1127469-fan-group-pdf?p=1138932#post1138932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we need to look at which organizations were already covered in other fan pieces. Example, the Carpenters vs the Lord Stewards. Are they the same group, and does that mean we don't need the Carpenters. Kings, your thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>They have similar themes, but folklore vs patrotism and American vs British are real differences.<br /> <br /> Personally I wouldn't worry about duplicates. There's no point in arguing about which group is better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 09-09-2017, 01:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T11:06:47-07:00","id":1138942,"title":"","content":"They mentioned that we could possible emphasize in Talents/Frailties just how vastly different these people are from the original personality, maybe some kind of physical change to go along with the personality shift.<br /> <br /> It's not about &quot;better&quot; so much as familiar ground. If we already have a group with the same themes/ideas, we don't need another. Like how you said the difference between the Carpenters vs the Stewards is &quot;Ancient Folklore&quot; vs &quot;Modern Patriotism&quot;, we should at least run down the groups we have and make sure that we don't have any heavy duplication, and if there is we pick the group that better emphasizes the themes being displayed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T12:01:47-07:00","id":1138957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1127469-fan-group-pdf?p=1138942#post1138942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They mentioned that we could possible emphasize in Talents/Frailties just how vastly different these people are from the original personality, maybe some kind of physical change to go along with the personality shift.</div> </div> </div> </div>But... Isn't that what we did?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1127469-fan-group-pdf?p=1138942#post1138942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not about &quot;better&quot; so much as familiar ground. If we already have a group with the same themes/ideas, we don't need another. Like how you said the difference between the Carpenters vs the Stewards is &quot;Ancient Folklore&quot; vs &quot;Modern Patriotism&quot;, we should at least run down the groups we have and make sure that we don't have any heavy duplication, and if there is we pick the group that better emphasizes the themes being displayed.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I meant was that, if we have two duplicates obviously we'd want to keep the better one of the two - and it just seems like it might be better to pick both than argue over which one is better.<br /> <br /> Especially if both authors are on this thread... admitedly not too likely.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 09-09-2017, 03:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T13:11:15-07:00","id":1138978,"title":"","content":"well, I have listed my groups that I really want to see (the ones which show up in Flyboy's original list and my top tier list), the groups I would like to see (the second tier of my list) and the groups that it would be a nice surprise to see, but not a must (all the rest I haven't wrote in my list). However, I see those as more of a guideline than anything absolute* and I give the project's editors the finale say, as I love my organizations and in a case I'll have to judge between them and another's creations, I won't be impartial :P<br /> <br /> *a special case are Raziel Ltd, R.A.M, Ebony Fangs, Pythian Oracles and the Nimrod Movement. Those five are ones I really wish to see in any such project as &quot;top tier&quot; orgs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-10T16:02:51-07:00","id":1139296,"title":"","content":"Okay, here's the drafts of the intros for the Compact and Conspiracy sections.<br /> <br /> As near as the scholars of the Vigil can tell, the earliest compacts were founded in the Fertile Crescent and Nile Delta as groups of hunters came together during the earliest foundations of civilization. Since then compacts have risen and faded with the tides of the Vigil, finding that forming bonds of mutual trust made them safer against the monsters than waiting for the inevitable revenge killings.<br /> <br /> For much of history the Vigil compacts tended to remain regional operations, restrained by geographical limitations and inabilities to quickly communicate with each other. Even today most compacts tend to restrict themselves to a single area, lacking the resources and numbers to match with the monsters over distances. More pointedly, compacts have tended to have specific memberships based on who founded them. One group founded the Bahamas was formed only from fishermen on the coasts who protected their homes against the creatures from the Caribbean\u2019s various blue holes. They outright refused several other hunters who tried to join from inland, believing that their lack of experience on the seas would be a dangerous hindrance to their typical Vigil.<br /> <br /> Compacts are fluid creatures; no two are alike. Some model themselves along paramilitary lines, with strict schedules and duties to perform. Others are little better than gangs, focused on a singular threat rather than any kind of overarching philosophy. However they are organized, the common thread is that there is no \u201ctypical\u201d compact, any more than a \u201ctypical\u201d monster.<br /> <br /> The largest struggle in a compact typically involves coordinating within itself. With the most famous being the example of the division between Null Mysteriis\u2019 Rationalists and Open-Minds, just because two groups fall under the same umbrella is no guarantee that they can see eye-to-eye. Many compacts have fallen to civil war, infighting becoming a fact of life rather than a temporary problem. A compact in Canada known as the Mountain Men were destroyed in the 1800s, the wedge issue whether or not they would accept native tribesmen into their number and their so-called \u201cheathen\u201d ways. As they fought, the creatures that stalked the Canadian wilderness ran about unimpeded until a special force of the North-West Mounted Police was formed to finally end the rampages with the assistance of the same communities the Mountain Men ignored.<br /> <br /> For all their faults, in regions where the major conspiracies have little presence compacts are the rallying point for the local Vigil. Lone cells in too deep and travelling hunters looking for assistance will contact the local compacts looking for help, as well as being sometimes-arbiters between various supernatural factions who want a go-between when they need a cease-fire or negotiation. No monster like each other, but hunters hate all monsters equally. This turns compacts into valuable balancing forces where they take root, for the sake of everyone living under their aegis. <hr />Conspiracies rightly believe that they are feared by all, human and monster alike. While some consider this a terrible fact, the conspiracies and their leadership see this as a useful tool. Monster or man, the mere appearance of the men in black or inquisition is often enough to make people shut up and do what they\u2019re told. The ones that don\u2019t are typically the ones that go missing and are never seen again.<br /> <br /> Conspiracies are often abused for the time it takes for them to organize, for the secrets they keep not only from the world, but from their own membership. These abuses ignore the reality of what the conspiracies must face each day. These conspiracies must contend with evils so ancient and great that most men can\u2019t begin to fathom them. Lost societies hidden beneath the Earth and under the waves. Beings from beyond space and within time that mock physics and mangle reality. Other, darker conspiracies aligned with the monsters with goals so depraved that their own sins pale in comparison. When the cells and compacts are overwhelmed and the monsters gain power, the conspiracies don\u2019t hear much complaining about secrets and deceptions from the hunters they pull from the fire.<br /> <br /> While internal struggles are just as evident as in a compact, the hunters at the level of a conspiracy know that there are bigger matters at stake than their own petty desires. The herd mentality is both a blessing and a curse for conspiracy hunters, as it gives them a leadership but also weights them with bureaucracy. While everyone loves to pin much of this stereotype on Task Force: VALKYRIE, several other conspiracies have their own stories to tell of toxic internal cultures. The Ascending Ones have had several cells under the Jagged Crescent go rogue, believing that with their drug money and access to alchemic elixirs they could strike out on their own without the weight of the Knife of Paradise or Southern Temple. More frightening, few of these rogue cells have ever been neutralized or brought back into the fold.<br /> <br /> Even if a conspiracy has been formed relatively recently, their files stretch back for centuries and their numbers are massive. Even conspiracies like the Lucifuge can count on numbers to overwhelm their most serious problems. Webs of informants and patsies act as the footsoldiers of the conspiracies, both providing disposable assets and a stable recruiting pool for those rare hunters who show the perfect mix of initiative, skepticism, and suspicion to fight for such massive organizations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-10T22:53:27-07:00","id":1139362,"title":"","content":"Two profession ideas.<br /> <br /> <b>Politician:</b> A &quot;big-picture&quot; player, able to act at any level of play by dint of the power they wield and the danger of killing one affecting the masquerade.<br /> <br /> <b>Operative</b><b>:</b> Spies and agents, slippery and able to work in the background with a good knowledge of surveillance and intelligence gathering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","val