?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-12T12:11:56-07:00","id":1139746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1127469-fan-group-pdf?p=1139737#post1139737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it probably has more to do with the fact that zombies are a different genera to the Underworld - post appoclpytic rather than dungeon crawl. Now I've had more time to think about it, it might be worth considering a fade to light grey at the top rather than a fade to pure white.</div> </div> </div> </div>well, for what it worth, when I looked at the picture I didn't thought about zombies or post apocalyptic horror- I've thought about the countless dead which send their hands to the light, desperate to get out- and yearning for every park of life they can put their hands on. In sort, something very ghostly, not zombie- like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-12T17:52:39-07:00","id":1139795,"title":"","content":"Here's what I've got for the intro to conspiracies.<br /> <br /> <b>Chapter 2: Conspiracies</b><br /> <br /> Conspiracies rightly believe that they are feared by all, human and monster alike. While some consider this a terrible fact, the conspiracies and their leadership see this as a useful tool. Monster or man, the mere appearance of the men in black or inquisition is often enough to make people shut up and do what they\u2019re told. The ones that don\u2019t are typically the ones that go missing and are never seen again.<br /> <br /> Conspiracies are often abused for the time it takes for them to organize, for the secrets they keep not only from the world, but from their own membership. These abuses ignore the reality of what the conspiracies must face each day. These conspiracies must contend with evils so ancient and great that most men can\u2019t begin to fathom them. Lost societies hidden beneath the Earth and under the waves. Beings from beyond space and within time that mock physics and mangle reality. Other, darker conspiracies aligned with the monsters with goals so depraved that their own sins pale in comparison. When the cells and compacts are overwhelmed and the monsters gain power, the conspiracies don\u2019t hear much complaining about secrets and deceptions from the hunters they pull from the fire.<br /> <br /> While internal struggles are just as evident as in a compact, the hunters at the level of a conspiracy know that there are bigger matters at stake than their own petty desires. The herd mentality is both a blessing and a curse for conspiracy hunters, as it gives them a leadership but also weights them with bureaucracy. While everyone loves to pin much of this stereotype on Task Force: VALKYRIE, several other conspiracies have their own stories to tell of toxic internal cultures. The Ascending Ones have had several cells under the Jagged Crescent go rogue, believing that with their drug money and access to alchemic elixirs they could strike out on their own without the weight of the Knife of Paradise or Southern Temple. More frightening, few of these rogue cells have ever been neutralized or brought back into the fold.<br /> <br /> Even if a conspiracy has been formed relatively recently, their files stretch back for centuries and their numbers are massive. Even conspiracies like the Lucifuge can count on numbers to overwhelm their most serious problems. Webs of informants and patsies act as the footsoldiers of the conspiracies, both providing disposable assets and a stable recruiting pool for those rare hunters who show the perfect mix of initiative, skepticism, and suspicion to fight for such massive organizations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T04:13:50-07:00","id":1139868,"title":"","content":"Hi im amer and i think the cat cult should be cut out even though i like it because instead of buying the endowment it increases by status and there's no 3ed status dot power and i think it's more micro template really in fact if the base power could ba base merit and other merits following just my opinion","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T17:30:13-07:00","id":1140046,"title":"","content":"We're more than happy to accept help Ameraaaaaa.<br /> <br /> Also, just added a factions section to SRO, thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T02:49:26-07:00","id":1140123,"title":"","content":"Thanks but ok so i want to try hunters any group without hunter","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T07:29:00-07:00","id":1140157,"title":"","content":"so Flyboy/Reaper/Aquastic- one you would decide which of my orgs pas the cut, could you inform me so I could finish their missing sections? I've thought about completing them all for the project, but my time is kinda limited between my job, my blog and my own homebrew and other projects, so I prefer to know that division in advance so I could divide my time more efficiently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-16T19:29:18-07:00","id":1140953,"title":"","content":"Okay, here's the initial idea for the Operative profession.<br /> <br /> <b>Operative</b><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cYou think you\u2019re part of the shadows? That\u2019s cute.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> Operatives are what most people think of when they think of the word \u201cspy\u201d, though that\u2019s a rather narrow idea of how to think of what an operator does. Some are what you could consider the classic \u201cspy\u201d, staking out targets of their nation\u2019s choosing to turn them into a source of information against their native government and paying them rather handsomely for it. Others are more what are known as \u201chandlers\u201d, the higher-level agents who oversee the teams of operatives that work out of their embassies and consulates. No nation is stupid enough to send their people over without first making sure they have diplomatic immunity in case something goes wrong.<br /> <br /> Their positions often mean they\u2019re some of the most endangered by the paranormal. As much as most monsters try to separate themselves from the lives they once lived, some feel that their abilities give them a chance to be the greatest patriots to their nations. Witches spells watch over sensitive buildings, using sympathetic magics to trace a traitor back to their handler. Vampiric powers can manipulate turned officials into patsies that could no longer care if their extramarital dalliances or corrupt deals are brought to light. Secretive supersoldier programs and ancient secrets all become the reasons some operatives join the Vigil.<br /> <br /> Your basic operative isn\u2019t made for a fight. More often, they\u2019re expected to remain to the rear or hidden under a cover and utilize information. Planting bugs, breaking and entering, even training in behavior analysis are all skills the best operatives have to bring to the Vigil. While many are in physical shape and may have even received weapons training, these are not the greatest skills they can bring to bear. If things go wrong, someone else bails them out if they can\u2019t escape on their own.<br /> <br /> Nearly all operatives are snapped up by conspiracies, as their unique skillsets can only be matched by a worthwhile compensation or orders from their national governments. Task Force: VALKYRIE suits are often operatives, especially for when a foreign posting is needed. MI18, the Lord Stewards, and Section 9 also make heavy use of intelligence operatives, primarily to keep an eye on their own nationals and study what other nations are doing in terms of the occult. Only a few compacts are able to keep up with an operative\u2019s needs, the Barrett Commission, Schutzgruppe 14, and the Bureau des Circonstances Extraordinaires the most prominent examples.<br /> <br /> Above all, an operative muse be unobtrusive. They aren\u2019t soldiers who crash into a warehouse guns blazing, or the techs who create the gear used on their operations. In fact, the highest compliment to be paid to an operative is simply, \u201cThey aren\u2019t smart enough to be a spy.\u201d<br /> <br /> <b>Concepts:</b> Embassy juggler; Press corps infiltrator; Headquarters workhorse; Cold War relic; Wetwork expert; Electronics whiz-kid; Legislative corrupter; Counter-Intel wizard; \u201cProblem Solver\u201d; Mercenary operator<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Stealth and Subterfuge<br /> <br /> <b>1:</b> Junior Agent<br /> <b>2:</b> Field Operative/Analyst<br /> <b>3:</b> Senior Operative/Senior Analyst<br /> <b>4:</b> Section Chief<br /> <b>5:</b> Deputy Director","signature":"","edited":{"userid":483,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","user":"Flyboy254","date":". 09-21-2017, 11:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-16T23:13:35-07:00","id":1140991,"title":"","content":"I have some proposed Hunters and Stereotypes for remaining factions. I'll post them here for approval by the original authors.<br /> <br /> Aki-Ten<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Hunters<br /> <br /> You thought studying computer science would be a way to get away from the family shrine and it's rituals. Technically you were right but twenty years of providing tech support to keep shikigami in their proper servers is starting to wear at your patience.<br /> <br /> The world moves too fast these days. No one takes their time to make sure things are done properly. Not you though, you're careful. You make sure to do the full rite not just the streamlined version the computer asks for. You think the shikigami appreciate your efforts.<br /> <br /> You're not of noble birth but you have a gift for summoning and binding Shikigami. Some of the more traditional older members of the conspiracy don't approve but you get results so they haven't done anything, yet.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> MI-18<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Hunters</b><br /> <br /> Your grandfather built gadgets for spies during the War but he always dreamed of more. Now you have a chance to do so, to be the unknown hero saving the world from a madman's death ray. Honestly though, you'd rather stay in the lab you don't really have the stomach for the action.<br /> <br /> You were offered a choice, hand over the plans to trans-dimensional vortex inducer and come do some government work or get a bullet. You chose the former but you're slowly rebuilding your old research. This time they won't laugh at you. This time you'll have your revenge.<br /> <br /> You're an old fashioned agent who's not afraid to get his hands dirty for Queen and Country. Your partner is a little less loyal, one of those &quot;boxed crooks&quot; as they're called. You know he's doing off the books research and that you'll have to kill him. It's a shame he's been a decent if erratic partner. It'll be a shame to see him go.<br /> <br /> <b>Stereotypes</b><br /> <br /> Haans-Chowhury Productions: We have reports of some Colonials in powered armour. As long as they keep those laser cannons pointed at alleged &quot;Alien Invaders&quot; we've agreed to look the other way.<br /> <br /> Lord Stewarts: Mad Scientists tend to be utterly ignorant of the occult. As such they sometimes run afoul Faeries, Werewolves, Vampires and what not. When that happens you'll be expected to babysit one of these bureaucrats while you clean up the mess.<br /> <br /> Taskforce Valkyrie: The Americans have never met a problem they haven't tried to shoot. Expect any operation to go to shit if they show up.<br /> <br /> Section Nine: The Cold War wasn't easy on anybody but at least our specialists in the weird stayed human. Some countries, can't say that.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9065,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9065-darkblade","user":"Darkblade","date":". 09-17-2017, 02:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9065-darkblade","name":"Darkblade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T01:30:25-07:00","id":1141006,"title":"","content":"I don't like being too critical, but MI18 keeps the mad scientists locked up in the mental asylum / labs, not on the front line. The actual hunters are more James Bond types, who'd casually kill a man in cold blood and laugh it off with a snappy one liner. They've had stereotypes since the start too.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar483_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"483\" data-vbnamecard=\"483\">Flyboy254</a> I like the write up, but the Lord Stewards wouldn't employ operatives directly. When they need spying done they'd ask for aid from an intelligence services.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T09:39:08-07:00","id":1141094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkblade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1127469-fan-group-pdf?p=1140991#post1140991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have some proposed Hunters and Stereotypes for remaining factions. I'll post them here for approval by the original authors.<br /> <br /> Aki-Ten<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think that the concepts themselves are fine- but there is a little misreading. The Shikigami aren't stored inside of a computer- instead, they are bound to magical Ofuda made of silicon, inscribed with occult spells which contain the spirit. Using the Projector, the Aki Ten hunter can translate the Shikigami into digital data and send it to another Projector, which encode the data into another Ofuda. They still haven't discover how to do &quot;copy paste&quot; to spirits, however- with such discovery would probably annoy many Werewolves in Japan :P I probably should have written more about how the Spirit Projector works- I'll do so once I'll have time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T11:48:54-07:00","id":1141142,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar134_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"134\" data-vbnamecard=\"134\">The Kings Raven</a> Feel free to be critical, that's why I'm posting them here rather than directly into the doc. With that criticism in mind I think I can salvage the reluctant descendant (make him grandson of a spy who'd rather be on the tech side of things) and the one with the bad partner (make the partner a tech attache) but the boxed scientist is obviously right out.<br /> <br /> How would an agent who specializes as placing themselves in the role of an &quot;igor&quot; before taking out their &quot;masters&quot; work?<br /> <br /> I should have checked the thread first to see if the Stereotypes just got lost in the transfer. My mistake. I copied those over for you now.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar503_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"503\" data-vbnamecard=\"503\">LostLight</a> Damn I really did like the disgruntled IT hunter concept but that doesn't mesh with the tech as described. Maybe they could repair broken Projectors?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9065-darkblade","name":"Darkblade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T12:07:50-07:00","id":1141158,"title":"","content":"well, maintaining the &quot;shikigami exchange network&quot; and the &quot;projection interface&quot; both relay on a computer network, so that hunter could still be an IT guy. That's why I've said that the concepts are fine- need some more flesh on their bones, but fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T13:44:36-07:00","id":1141186,"title":"","content":"So, here's a question. What's the big differences between the Aki Ten and Les Mysteries?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T13:45:52-07:00","id":1141189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1127469-fan-group-pdf?p=1141186#post1141186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, here's a question. What's the big differences between the Aki Ten and Les Mysteries?</div> </div> </div> </div>If I understand correctly, the ability to transfer control of the sites digitally","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T13:56:37-07:00","id":1141196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1127469-fan-group-pdf?p=1141186#post1141186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, here's a question. What's the big differences between the Aki Ten and Les Mysteries?</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot, actually?<br /> <br /> The Les Mysteres serve the spirits- they serve as a bridge between humanity and the spirit world. They dance with demons and angels, gods and archetypes. They serve as a channel, allowing themselves to be possessed by the Shadow, while serving their patrons on the side of Flesh. They maintain that harmony between man and spirit, and hunt for the Forsaken, for they defile that complicated relationship by severing Flesh from Spirit.<br /> <br /> The Aki Ten, however, are not shamans, nor are they mediums. They do not serve the spirit world, and they do not seek balance with its denizens. They want to rule it, force it to their will and use their power upon the spirit world to serve humanity. Hisil is a wild realm, and it should be tamed, maintained and bound so it would serve mankind. They want to conquer the Shadow specifically and the supernatural world in general. Their Endowments reflect it- they aren't possessed by the spirit, but they summon bound shikigami to fight and die in their battles. Its not companionship- its servitude. When a Les Mysteres hunter hear about a great spirit which has awakened and pose a threat upon the world, they seek to negotiate with it and return the world to harmony. When an Aki Ten hears about it, the first thing they'll think is &quot;how can I bind that ancient god to my will?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T14:35:45-07:00","id":1141213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkblade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1127469-fan-group-pdf?p=1141142#post1141142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar134_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"134\" data-vbnamecard=\"134\">The Kings Raven</a> Feel free to be critical, that's why I'm posting them here rather than directly into the doc. With that criticism in mind I think I can salvage the reluctant descendant (make him grandson of a spy who'd rather be on the tech side of things) and the one with the bad partner (make the partner a tech attache) but the boxed scientist is obviously right out.</div> </div> </div> </div> For MI18 hunters the absolute must is that they're perfect gentlemen. If you haven't seen Kingsman watch it. The second thing to bear in mind is that they play very very dirty.<br /> <br /> This juxtiposition is key. An MI18 member should make slitting a defenceless Russian hacker's throat while she sleeps look suave and sophisticated. Their sample hunters should explore these themes. Some ideas off the top of my head.<ul><li>A former football hooligan who thinks that the upper class aren't any better, they just hide it well.</li> <li>Someone who's seen too much horror on the job and is a bit of an empty shell. But he acts polite and sophisticated because he wishes he was a gentleman of leasure.</li> <li>Someone who really is the ideal English gentleman, and is having trouble squaring his upbringing with the demands of the job. And has started to adopt philosophical ideas from mad scientists to help solve the dissonance.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkblade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1127469-fan-group-pdf?p=1141142#post1141142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I should have checked the thread first to see if the Stereotypes just got lost in the transfer. My mistake. I copied those over for you now.</div> </div> </div> </div> There's a reason I suggest copying them over from the threads at the very end of this project <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> - or at least check the dates with the last edited date on the forums. I like to tinker.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkblade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1127469-fan-group-pdf?p=1141142#post1141142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Damn I really did like the disgruntled IT hunter concept but that doesn't mesh with the tech as described. Maybe they could repair broken Projectors?</div> </div> </div> </div>Have a look at my Reality Hackers. They already have a hunters section, but you could add an extra.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T14:40:33-07:00","id":1141214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1127469-fan-group-pdf?p=1141196#post1141196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;How can I bind that ancient god to my will?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, but how in-line is this with the ideas behind Onmyodo?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T22:40:31-07:00","id":1141324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1127469-fan-group-pdf?p=1141214#post1141214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, but how in-line is this with the ideas behind Onmyodo?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) they aren't the Onmyodo- they are wanna be Onmyodo. Their views are as much influenced by pop culture as much as real history<br /> 2)we are talking about an organization which has used any means necessary (including violence) in order to get monopoly over occult and fortune telling, and that the principle view of making a shikigami is not &quot;communing&quot; as much as it is &quot;binding and manipulating&quot;. I think we are ok.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T12:15:58-07:00","id":1141484,"title":"","content":"Added some information for the Carpenters, Enemies and some information for Members.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T12:26:00-07:00","id":1141488,"title":"","content":"I also just want to note that if for some reason you don't want to put the Aki Ten (or any other organization) in the book, its fun- I just wanted to clarify that the way I see it, there is very little resemblance between them and the Les Mysteres. It has just occurred to me that my posts may have been a bit cranky, but I wrote them when I was really tired and when I've just woke up (late) to work, so sorry if they sounded a bit rude or anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T12:38:49-07:00","id":1141492,"title":"","content":"I'm just worried about making sure that if we include real belief systems in the books, they should (somewhat) hem to the actual system of worship/occultism they draw from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T13:13:19-07:00","id":1141512,"title":"","content":"well, while I did preformed a research when I wrote them (including reading an essay about the history and beliefs on the Onmyodo and doing a class about Japanese culture, history and aesthetics in my university), I have used some artistic freedom for their modern incarnation (I have said a number of times in their writeup that even in the setting they aren't the &quot;true Onmyodo&quot; as much as they are a modern creation formed by a number of powerful families which mixed up with people who were inspired by them- hence their tension with Japan's mages). I don't think I have portrayed them too different than any way modern Japanese pop culture does, and besides- that belief system is, technically, dead. Any connection between the original tradition and the people who call themselves onmyoji in modern time is very thin, more or less the connection between those hunters and the original tradition. I also don't remember reading anywhere that the Onmyodo has much emphasis about communing with the spirits like mediums- they were more about fortune telling and exorcism, with the responsibility of talking with the spirits directly being something much less &quot;noble&quot; and in the responsibility of the miko (as the Azusa Miko are in the setting).<br /> <br /> Again, there isn't a lot of information about the belief system itself- at least, I haven't found such. I have done the best I can with what I did, but I don't think they are too far away from the actual Onmyodo- sure, there are differences, but the reason for those is found in their writeup. In real life, the Onmyodo practically died during the Meiji Restoration- but what if, in the CofD, the shattered pieces of that organization has somehow preserved themselves until not only that they survived in the modern world, but actually survived by adapting themselves to it, at any cost it may take? That's what I wished to discover with the New Way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 09-18-2017, 04:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T14:35:01-07:00","id":1141545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1127469-fan-group-pdf?p=1141492#post1141492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just worried about making sure that if we include real belief systems in the books, they should (somewhat) hem to the actual system of worship/occultism they draw from.</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh oh...<br /> <br /> I'm kidding <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Hakollel are (from my limited understanding of theology) rather blasphemous. But that's intentional, you're supposed to ask if Hakollel are cutting edge Rabbi's who's discovery of formally lost lore means they know better than other Rabbi's or if they've succumbed to hubris out of a desire for miracles on demand. Hubris is as much a part of rabbinical lore as Awakening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T20:05:57-07:00","id":1141633,"title":"","content":"Roger that. Anyway, can one of you guys get a look at the edits made to SRO and Carpenters?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T20:29:49-07:00","id":1141638,"title":"","content":"<b>Quick update from me:</b><br /> <br /> My laptop has fully-died on me, which has affected my general mood and stress levels for this month so my output will be severely diminished. Will continue to work on art when I get the chance.<br /> <br /> <br /> Currently doing another once-over to figure out what can be safely pushed back and what should be pushed forward. There are a few unfinished organizations whose writers are not active in this thread.For now, these can be safely left on <b>STANDBY </b>until further notice:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>COMPACTS</b><br /> The Bookhounds of London (atamajakki), currently missing Status<br /> The Fire Starters (Killer300), currently missing Status<br /> The Parabalani (terpsichordean), currently missing Hunters<br /> The Underworld Syndicate (THE WRITER IS CURRENTLY UNKNOWN), currently missing Hunters<br /> Venerators of the Old Gods (wyrdhamster), currently missing Status<br /> <br /> <b>CONSPIRACIES</b><br /> The Fog Men (atamajakki), currently missing Status and Endowments<br /> The Oakley Institute (Almarck), currently missing Enemies and Stereotypes<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> That takes out 7 organizations. If we also take out the organizations that Lostlight greenlit as okay-to-be-excluded, that takes out another 8, totaling in 5 Compacts, 7 Conspiracies, and 3 Cults. This makes the running total of(I made a huge counting mistake somewhere before in my last numbers update),<b>14/27 Compacts, 20/44 Conspiracies </b>and <b>6/20 Cults/Cabals, </b>including the recent changes to SRO and the Carpenters. We can definitely finish out the Cults as is but we should probably consider cuts to at least the Conspiracies.<br /> <br /> <br /> For the Conspiracies, I'm making a note that we're most-likely going to keep organizations that are close-to-completion. The list that I made previously should still hold up so these following organizations (missing only one section sans Factions) are considered <b>SAFE TO KEEP</b> for now. This should bring the number of expected completions to <b>18 Compacts</b>, <b>32 Conspiracies</b>, and <b>9 Cults</b>.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>COMPACTS</b><br /> Maagal HaBaal VehaAshera<br /> Maw of the River<br /> Shepherds of Annwn<br /> Sunrise Securities<br /> <br /> <b>CONSPIRACIES</b><br /> al-Rih al-Asuad<br /> Burya Storozh<br /> Followers of Set<br /> Heirs of the Crown<br /> Her Majesty's Royal Order of Supernatural Defenders<br /> KSI 21<br /> Navio de Tolos<br /> The Nibiru<br /> Tiensheng<br /> The Usij<br /> Yam VeHar Factories<br /> The Zmei Initiative<br /> <br /> <b>CULTS ETC</b><br /> The Knights Errant<br /> Hearth of Hestia<br /> Los Innocentes<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar503_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"503\" data-vbnamecard=\"503\">LostLight</a> Insofar, the Pythian Oracles, the Ebony Fangs, R.A.M., and Raziel Ltd have made the cut and are considered finished; the Nimrod Movement needs the Enemies and Hunters sections (as well as Factions but it's not 100% necessary). Off of your list, the Compacts Sabaoth and the Theatre of Tragedies are short of being considered close-to-completion, as well as the Conspiracy Mori Kage. The other organizations on your list should be considered <b>SAFE</b>. Of organizations that have been added that aren't on your list:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Missing One Section</b><br /> Shepherds of Annwn<br /> Burya Storozh<br /> The Followers of Set<br /> Tiensheng<br /> The Usij<br /> <br /> <b>Missing Two Sections</b><br /> The Silent Imperative<br /> Cage of Shadows<br /> Chasseurs de Tetes<br /> Custodes Ignis<br /> Hrt Ifset<br /> Knights of the Bloody Chalice<br /> Lycos Agema<br /> Penyihir Mayat<br /> Scharlach Spinnwebe<br /> Silentium<br /> Tartaruchi<br /> Tatau o te Po<br /> <br /> Anything else is missing more than two.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> To your discretion, we should consider cutting things that weren't on your list. I don't know which ones have higher priority so that is entirely to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1417,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","user":"Reaper Verse","date":". 09-18-2017, 11:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T07:38:58-07:00","id":1141741,"title":"","content":"Take your time Reaper, we aren't exactly on a time limit here after all.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b> Politician profession up!<br /> <br /> <b>Politician</b><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cWe have a saying in Gaffney. \u2018Shake with your right hand, hold a rock in your left.\u2019\u201d</i><br /> <br /> To be a professional in your field is one thing. Being a career politician is something different entirely. Finances, law, education, land management, all have to be rolled into one singular package in order to get anything done. Deals must be made, wheels need greasing, and sometimes you just need to force someone to see it your way or no way at all.<br /> <br /> Then you add in the other problems of the world. Vampires trying to control the money in a city, witches doing their best to use townships as their own personal magic testing grounds, even groups of so-called \u201chunters\u201d using the people in a region as patsies and fall-guys. That isn\u2019t how government is supposed to work, or if it is it\u2019s supposed to only happen for the people who are in charge.<br /> <br /> Politicians are of course learned in political science, and many make it a point to realize some education in areas they care deeply about, such as educational or environmental issues. This makes any politician skilled in academic research methods, provided it\u2019s on a subject they support. It also helps that they often have a host of social connections capable of giving them the necessary support to bring their plans to fruition. This makes them adept social movers and capable academics, if only in a limited fashion.<br /> <br /> For the Vigil, a politician is everyone\u2019s favorite ally. Even on a local level, they have enough pull with local authorities to make it so investigations can quietly die down or focus an investigator on another matter. Politicians in the know can be even more dangerous against a monster than any well-armed hunter, since they at least know what to look out for when a monster tries to take control over them in their own office.<br /> <br /> Politicians typically find themselves working closely with the Barret Commission against the actions of vampires in their cities and counties, though they also can find themselves working alongside the Union if they find themselves in need of votes. Most conspiracies actually prefer to keep politicians at arms-length due to their relatively higher profile compared to more \u201cworking-class\u201d hunters,<br /> <br /> Rank 1: Alderman/Local supervior<br /> Rank 2: City Council/County Commision<br /> Rank 3: Mayor/State Legislator<br /> Rank 4: State Senator/Congressman<br /> Rank 5: Senator<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Politics and Persuasion<br /> <br /> <b>Concepts:</b> Kindly mayor; Firebrand independent; Backroom manipulator; Legislative magician; Conservative crusader; Jovial representative; Lobbyist\u2019s best friend; Hand-shaking baby-kisser; Policy wonk; Vengeful power-seeker","signature":"","edited":{"userid":483,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","user":"Flyboy254","date":". 09-19-2017, 08:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T10:44:46-07:00","id":1142590,"title":"","content":"A second draft on the Aki Ten MI-18 hunters<br /> <br /> Aki Ten<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> You thought studying computer science would be an exciting path to success. A master of cutting edge Virtual Reality technology you'd have built a name for yourself. Or you would have had your VR startup not been bought out by the Aki Ten as investors abandoned you in the early 90s. Now you spend your days monitoring the projector device network for security vulnerabilities and watch other men use your technology to control Gods. That should have been you.<br /> <br /> The world moves too fast these days. No one has any respect for tradition or making sure things are done properly. Not you though, you're careful. You make sure to do the full rite not just the streamlined version the computer asks for. It takes longer, a fact your cellmates have bemoaned after many a battle, but the Shikigami seem to appreciate your efforts. At least they seem to serve you more readily than your more modern coworkers.<br /> <br /> You don't think you're of noble birth at least you can't prove that you are. Your family history has been lost. Yet you have a gift for summoning and binding Shikigami. Some of the more traditional older members of the conspiracy view you as a threat. A young upstart here to take their rightful place. You have no such ambitions and are quite happy to serve under them but they have been growing ever more spiteful with you.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> MI-18<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Hunters</b><br /> <br /> Your grandfather was one of the greatest agents that British Intelligence had ever known. Your father while not as great was well regarded for his service. The Boy's Club mentality of the agency expects great things from you as well. Unfortunately you don't seem to have inherited their knack for espionage. You do have the raw physical talent and have trained with the best but you can't stand the sight of blood and intensely dislike violence. You managed to play it cool through training but you'll be receiving your first assignment soon. You're not sure you'll be able to keep up this facade.<br /> <br /> Every Mad Scientist wants a beautiful assistant. That's where you come in. You approach suspected Mad Scientists and integrate yourself into their life. Most were the sort of boys who had no hopes of even talking to a girl like you. They never see it coming when you put them down. If only the boys upstairs could appreciate your work, you've been due for a promotion for years now. The gentlemen that they are they'd never say it to your face but you know they don't consider you fit to even have your current position.<br /> <br /> As an English Gentleman you're expected to keep a stiff upper lip and always maintain a poised and sophisticated outlook on any situation. You do your best but the things you've seen; a man in Frankfurt meticulously stitching together murdered prostitutes to make his ideal lover, a cult in Dubai wiring people's brains into a massive analog computer, swarms of all consuming, self-replicating nanomachines nearly descending upon Cartif. You'd like to forget it all and just live out a normal life in ((Rich British Neighborhood Here)) but retirement isn't an option for an agent of the crown.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9065-darkblade","name":"Darkblade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T11:52:34-07:00","id":1142630,"title":"","content":"Now I'm wondering. Kings, what do the Lord Stewards and MI18 have on the death of Diana?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T06:26:41-07:00","id":1142877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkblade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1127469-fan-group-pdf?p=1142590#post1142590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A second draft on the Aki Ten MI-18 hunters<br /> <br /> Aki Ten<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> You thought studying computer science would be an exciting path to success. A master of cutting edge Virtual Reality technology you'd have built a name for yourself. Or you would have had your VR startup not been bought out by the Aki Ten as investors abandoned you in the early 90s. Now you spend your days monitoring the projector device network for security vulnerabilities and watch other men use your technology to control Gods. That should have been you.<br /> <br /> The world moves too fast these days. No one has any respect for tradition or making sure things are done properly. Not you though, you're careful. You make sure to do the full rite not just the streamlined version the computer asks for. It takes longer, a fact your cellmates have bemoaned after many a battle, but the Shikigami seem to appreciate your efforts. At least they seem to serve you more readily than your more modern coworkers.<br /> <br /> You don't think you're of noble birth at least you can't prove that you are. Your family history has been lost. Yet you have a gift for summoning and binding Shikigami. Some of the more traditional older members of the conspiracy view you as a threat. A young upstart here to take their rightful place. You have no such ambitions and are quite happy to serve under them but they have been growing ever more spiteful with you.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>look nice. I approve.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T07:59:28-07:00","id":1142904,"title":"","content":"Much better Darkblade. I think the one with the woman is a bit too on the nose though. MI18 should portray gentleman-hood in a positive way, otherwise the contrast between a refined gentleman and dirty espionage looses it's punch. Harry Dresden's chivalry might be a good model for how to handle their more outdated attitudes - well meaning but ultimately condescending.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Your grandfather was one of the greatest agents that British Intelligence had ever known. Your father while not as great was well regarded for his service. The Boy's Club mentality of the agency expects great things from you as well. Unfortunately you don't seem to have inherited their knack for espionage. You do have the raw physical talent and have trained with the best but you can't stand the sight of blood and intensely dislike violence. You managed to play it cool through training but you'll be receiving your first assignment soon. You're not sure you'll be able to keep up this facade.<br /> <br /> This technology is ancient, and it was built by madmen so nobody could figure out how to modernise it even if there was the budget to do so. There used to be a whole team of technicians, and soldiers on standby. But budget cut after budget cut hit, and now it's just you and sometimes the boy from the Chinese take out next door watching tape drives spin and lights blink in endless monotony. Until today, today the machine is spitting out warnings. You've made the call, London can have people here in three hours, according to these readings you have one. There's still old equipment gathering dust down here, Queen and Country call.<br /> <br /> Give a man enough power and he starts thinking with something other than his brain. Gold diggers and star struck groupies are common. You are refined, elegant and educated. Someone a foreign government official or shady titan of industry might invest time into acquiring. Naturally it ends with you stabbing them in the back, or just drugging them and rifling through their files. All's fair in love and politics.<br /> <br /> As an English Gentleman you're expected to keep a stiff upper lip and always maintain a poised and sophisticated outlook on any situation. You do your best but the things you've seen; a man in Frankfurt meticulously stitching together murdered prostitutes to make his ideal lover, a cult in Dubai wiring people's brains into a massive analog computer, swarms of all consuming, self-replicating nanomachines nearly descending upon Cartif. You'd like to forget it all and just live out a normal life in the countryside but nobility obliges an agent of the crown.<br /> <br /> You were recruited straight off the streets after blundering into an active investigation and handling yourself better than anyone expected. MI18 washed off the alcohol, put you into a Savile Row suit and sent you off to basic training and finishing schools. You think the manners and formality is a bit of a joke, the people here are twice as vicious as any of the football hooligans you used to socialise with. But you have to admit, you like the way you look in a suit.<br /> <br /> You've seen so many horrors, you've committed so many yourself, that it's hollowed you out. The charm, the manners, the snappy one liners, they're all a shield that's remained long after everything it was supposed to protect wasted away. But perhaps they still serve a purpose, every time some bio-engineered plague or Ancient Egyptian curse is diverted from the public your smooth received pronunciation and wit keep the ministers calm and the public blissfully unaware.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1127469-fan-group-pdf?p=1142630#post1142630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I'm wondering. Kings, what do the Lord Stewards and MI18 have on the death of Diana?</div> </div> </div> </div>MI-18 have the truth.<br /> <br /> The Lord Stewards have a fairly good idea of the supernatural effects her death had (on the Shadow, etc)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 09-23-2017, 06:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T18:23:57-07:00","id":1143635,"title":"","content":"So, do any Conspiracies have Endowments related to?<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Enhancing the Abjuration and Exorcism rules to apply to more monsters.</li> <li>Installing Occult/Cybernetic Malware into monsters and remote piloting them.</li> <li>Tapping Goetic archetypes (and their own Oneric Daemons/Goetia) to strengthen themselves.</li> <li>Invoking the weight of a monsters own crimes/victims against them.</li> </ol>I know they Les Mysteres use Spirits similarly to 3. I'm asking specifically about Goetics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T21:12:19-07:00","id":1143660,"title":"","content":"Well I'm not sure about 1, 2, and 3, but the Malleus and Lucifuge already had powers capable of doing both really, so I don't think they were included. What were you thinking?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T21:30:14-07:00","id":1143665,"title":"","content":"Not as an Endowment, but the Ebony Fangs do gain a Status bonus for Abjuring ghosts. As for Goetic archetypes, that's one of the interpretations for the Heirs of the Crown's Endowment, and is also the principle behind how the Navio use theirs, but it may not be exactly what you are looking for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-25T03:49:11-07:00","id":1143722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1127469-fan-group-pdf?p=1143660#post1143660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well I'm not sure about 1, 2, and 3, but the Malleus and Lucifuge already had powers capable of doing both really, so I don't think they were included. What were you thinking?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I had a few powers/Endowment ideas, but I wanted to make sure they weren't duplicating other work. I figured this grand compilation thread would be the place to ask, since the major Hunter fan contributors are already here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1127469-fan-group-pdf?p=1143665#post1143665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not as an Endowment, but the Ebony Fangs do gain a Status bonus for Abjuring ghosts. As for Goetic archetypes, that's one of the interpretations for the Heirs of the Crown's Endowment, and is also the principle behind how the Navio use theirs, but it may not be exactly what you are looking for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. So 3 is already covered, then. For 1, I was thinking more &quot;use X rules against Y creature now&quot; like being able to Abjure Vampires, Bind Horrors, or Exorcise the spells of Mages/Witches, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-25T04:03:14-07:00","id":1143725,"title":"","content":"So there's similarities between okeley institution and also the ake ten sorry if i got name wrong so what we do about it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-01T19:51:26-07:00","id":1145955,"title":"","content":"Well. after having recovered most of the files on my laptop and completing my basic education test to be certified as a substitute teacher, I have actually made a splash art. Hopefully, I will have some more time in the future while I am waiting for my results to come in.<br /> <br /> Until then, here is the Splash Art for the Pythian Oracles.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/xpSZvYF.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ameraaaaaa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1127469-fan-group-pdf?p=1143725#post1143725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So there's similarities between okeley institution and also the ake ten sorry if i got name wrong so what we do about it</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There is actually a fair amount of distinction between the Oakley Institute and the Aki Ten. Their source material is a big factor; the Oakley Institute references the Pokemon series whereas the Aki Ten references Tokyo Raven and Mahouka. The Oakley Institute is a tech-heavy organization that focuses on more animalistic creatures and beasts while the Aki Ten are a religion/spiritual-focused organization that uses tech to capture ephemeral creatures, mainly spirits. The Oakley Institute was ravaged by what is implied to be Angels and Demons so their current operations are held by the remnants of the original organization while the Aki Ten are a slowly growing power within Japan.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, the state of completion is what dictates what is safe and what isn't. LostLight has been actively updating Aki Ten, enough that the organization is ultimately complete. With the Oakley Institute, Almarck has not updated the organization for a while and I believe no one has decided if they want to take up the mantle and continue fleshing out the organization.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T05:21:43-07:00","id":1146032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1127469-fan-group-pdf?p=1145955#post1145955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well. after having recovered most of the files on my laptop and completing my basic education test to be certified as a substitute teacher, I have actually made a splash art. Hopefully, I will have some more time in the future while I am waiting for my results to come in.<br /> <br /> Until then, here is the Splash Art for the Pythian Oracles.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/xpSZvYF.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> There is actually a fair amount of distinction between the Oakley Institute and the Aki Ten. Their source material is a big factor; the Oakley Institute references the Pokemon series whereas the Aki Ten references Tokyo Raven and Mahouka. The Oakley Institute is a tech-heavy organization that focuses on more animalistic creatures and beasts while the Aki Ten are a religion/spiritual-focused organization that uses tech to capture ephemeral creatures, mainly spirits. The Oakley Institute was ravaged by what is implied to be Angels and Demons so their current operations are held by the remnants of the original organization while the Aki Ten are a slowly growing power within Japan.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, the state of completion is what dictates what is safe and what isn't. LostLight has been actively updating Aki Ten, enough that the organization is ultimately complete. With the Oakley Institute, Almarck has not updated the organization for a while and I believe no one has decided if they want to take up the mantle and continue fleshing out the organization.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok hi thanks for replying so yeah i don't think i can do the conspiracy well and what about basts group because it's rules don't fit with how endowments are made to work with status determining the benefits but otherwise I like the group","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T11:41:29-07:00","id":1146112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ameraaaaaa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1127469-fan-group-pdf?p=1146032#post1146032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok hi thanks for replying so yeah i don't think i can do the conspiracy well and what about basts group because it's rules don't fit with how endowments are made to work with status determining the benefits but otherwise I like the group</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Honestly, Bastet's Beloved is fine. There are very few groups that actually buck the trend when it comes to how the general formula goes (the only other one is the DiFillipo Family as they merge their Factions with their Status. For Bastet's Beloved, the implication is that players cannot actually purchase their Endowment dots; rather, they gain dots in their Endowment by gaining Status in the organization. While it may seem odd, it's mostly fine due to the fact that Bastet's Beloved do not receive an additional bonus for their 3rd Status dot and because the group overall is rather odd even by Hunter standards. Also, instead of being a Compact or Conspiracy, Bastet's Beloved are a Convention, so they really are kind of an outlier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T12:56:37-07:00","id":1146135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1127469-fan-group-pdf?p=1145955#post1145955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well. after having recovered most of the files on my laptop and completing my basic education test to be certified as a substitute teacher, I have actually made a splash art. Hopefully, I will have some more time in the future while I am waiting for my results to come in.<br /> <br /> Until then, here is the Splash Art for the Pythian Oracles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looks great, Reaper! I approve <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (also- congratulation!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T15:51:40-07:00","id":1146179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1127469-fan-group-pdf?p=1146112#post1146112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Bastet's Beloved, the implication is that players cannot actually purchase their Endowment dots; rather, they gain dots in their Endowment by gaining Status in the organization.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much.<br /> <br /> The way it works is that Status and their Endowment are basically the same thing. Instead of hearing on the social grapevine that Alice is trustworthy or the chief promoting Alice they sense the relative strength of eachother's Endowment to see who's higher ranked. So in the end it's arbitrary which one you buy and which one you get free.<br /> <br /> Anyway, going by likes I think the Beloved are the most popular group I wrote, so we should definitely include them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T22:37:02-07:00","id":1146260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1127469-fan-group-pdf?p=1146179#post1146179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty much.<br /> <br /> The way it works is that Status and their Endowment are basically the same thing. Instead of hearing on the social grapevine that Alice is trustworthy or the chief promoting Alice they sense the relative strength of eachother's Endowment to see who's higher ranked. So in the end it's arbitrary which one you buy and which one you get free.<br /> <br /> Anyway, going by likes I think the Beloved are the most popular group I wrote, so we should definitely include them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It might be good to add a sentence in the Endowments that makes it more explicit. It's definitely heavily implied but stating it outright makes it more definite and obvious.<br /> <br /> <br /> Here's another art: The Ebony Fangs.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/AQ55Hww.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" 